// SMT Divergence + Volume Profile + Anchored VWAP + Iceberg [v3.6]
// Smart Money Technique (multi-symbol divergence) + session Volume Profile
// with previous-session levels, naked POC tracking, confluence alerts, status
// dashboard, session-anchored VWAP with σ bands, and iceberg/absorption
// detection.
//
// v1.0 — SMT divergence (multi-symbol, confirmed-pivot based).
// v1.1 — Volume Profile with developing POC/VAH/VAL + histogram; Pine v6
//        syntax fixes; div tooltip with values; pivot-marker toggle.
// v1.2 — Previous-session fixed POC/VAH/VAL lines; naked POC tracking with
//        auto-removal on touch; confluence-aware SMT alerts; status table
//        dashboard.
// v1.3 — Session-anchored VWAP + σ bands (1σ/2σ/3σ, optional fill); live
//        realtime projection (current-bar tick data added on top of confirmed
//        accumulation); plot-break at session start; AVWAP/σ levels added to
//        confluence detection and the dashboard.
// v1.4 — Iceberg / absorption detection (volume × range × close-position
//        proxy for hidden iceberg-order footprints); optional confluence
//        gating against VP and AVWAP levels; bull/bear bias from close
//        position; rich tooltip with vol/range/close stats; dashboard rows
//        for session count and last event.
// v1.5 — Verified bug-fix release:
//        • Naked-POC grace period now actually works. The 1-bar grace check
//          was previously comparing `bar_index` against `prevSessStartBar`
//          (the start bar of the prior session, far in the past), so the
//          condition was effectively always true and a new session's
//          first-bar straddle could immediately invalidate a just-created
//          nPOC. Now stores `bar_index` (creation bar) in a dedicated
//          `nakedPOCCreationBars` array.
//        • SMT alert + dashboard dedup per pivot bar. Previously, a pivot
//          that diverged against all three comparison symbols fired three
//          separate alerts and the dashboard would only show whichever
//          symbol happened to be evaluated last (sym3), losing context for
//          the other two. Now collects all diverging symbols on the pivot,
//          fires ONE combined alert ("Bearish SMT vs ES1!, NQ1!, YM1! | ..."),
//          and updates dashboard state once.
//        • VP histogram redraw gated to once-per-bar-change-or-close instead
//          of every realtime tick. Bins only update on `barstate.isconfirmed`,
//          so the previous every-tick delete-and-rebuild of ~24 boxes
//          produced identical output. Tracked via `lastVpDrawBar` var.
// v3.6 — Fix runtime error RE10026 on 1-minute charts.
//        Reported: "Error on bar 5738: Bar index value of the `x1`
//        argument (0) in `line.new()` is too far from the current bar
//        index." Pine refuses an xloc.bar_index drawing coordinate that
//        sits more than ~max_bars_back bars before the current bar.
//        Several drawings anchor their LEFT edge at a session-start bar:
//          • prev-session POC/VAH/VAL lines + naked-POC line
//            → anchored at prevSessStartBar (can be 0 — the first
//              session starts at bar_index 0)
//          • composite POC/VAH/VAL lines → anchored at the OLDEST of up
//            to 5 tracked sessions' start bars
//          • developing POC/VAH/VAL lines, HVN/LVN lines, heatmap +
//            HVN-zone boxes → anchored at vpSessStart
//          • SMT divergence line → anchored at the previous pivot bar
//        On higher timeframes a session holds few bars so the anchor
//        stays close and the error never appears. On a 1-minute chart a
//        single session is ~1440 bars and the composite span is
//        ~5×1440 — easily past the limit, so 1-min charts crash.
//        Fix: new `safeLeftBar()` helper clamps any left x-coordinate to
//        `max(b, bar_index - 4900)`. Applied at the `lineLeft` and
//        `compLineLeft` definitions (covers all the redraw-block and
//        composite drawings in one place each) and at the prev-session /
//        naked-POC / SMT-divergence line sites. Every affected drawing
//        either uses extend.right or is a horizontal level reference, so
//        clamping the left anchor only shortens the drawn segment — the
//        price level shown is unchanged. No visible difference on
//        higher timeframes (the clamp never binds there).
//        Known remaining edge (not fixed): the Developing POC Trail
//        polyline builds chart.point.from_index points across the whole
//        session; on a Weekly/Monthly anchor + intraday chart its
//        oldest point could also exceed the limit. It is opt-in
//        (default off) and safe on Daily anchor, so deferred.
// v3.5 — Three real fixes from a large combined review (~23 items; the
//        other ~20 were verified non-bugs and rejected — see notes).
//        Fix 1 — recomputeBinsFromRaw runtime-crash guard. It accessed
//        `high[offset]` back to session start; on a Daily anchor with
//        a <=15s chart, or a Weekly/Monthly anchor on any intraday
//        timeframe, a session exceeds 5000 bars — `high[offset]` past
//        max_bars_back throws a runtime error. Now clamps the lookback
//        to 4999. On those extreme configs the profile covers only the
//        most-recent 5000 bars (degraded, documented) instead of crashing.
//        Fix 2 — doji / neutral-bar bearish bias in VP sentiment. The
//        bin classifier was a bool: `barBull = close > open`. An exact
//        doji (close==open) is `false` → its whole volume was dumped
//        into the bear side; same for a mid-range close under Buying
//        Pressure. Now a 3-state fraction: bull→1.0, bear→0.0,
//        neutral→0.5 (splits 50/50). Consistent with the v2.1
//        doji-neutral fix already applied to iceberg classification.
//        Affects vpBins/vpBinsBull, prev-POC sentiment tags, and the
//        dashboard Bull%/Bear% row.
//        Fix 3 — recomputeComposite merge optimised O(N·R²) → O(N·R).
//        The session-bin → composite-grid merge scanned all vpRows
//        composite bins for every source bin. A source bin only
//        overlaps a contiguous 1-3 bin run — now computed directly via
//        floor-division (±1 pad + clamp for FP safety; the overlap>0
//        test filters slack). Worst case drops ~128k → ~3k ops per
//        session-finalize. Not a crash risk before, just wasteful.
//        REJECTED review claims (verified non-bugs): AVWAP "double-count"
//        (the confirmed/live blocks are mutually exclusive on
//        barstate.isconfirmed); "zero-range session" (the finalize block
//        is guarded by vpSessHigh>vpSessLow AND fTotalV>0); "gapped-feed
//        bar range" (bar_index is contiguous over existing bars — no gap
//        inflation); "nPOC zero grace" (`> created` protects exactly the
//        creation bar = first bar of new session, which IS the 1-bar
//        grace); "SMT inverse compares mismatched metrics" (comparing the
//        cmp's low at consecutive chart-HIGH pivots is correct SMT); "VA
//        tie bias" (exact float ties are rare; tie-breaking is a defensible
//        choice); "InVA dead zone" (reviewer's arithmetic is wrong —
//        price at VAL+1.0 with td=2.5 IS within td); "SMT state updated
//        unconditionally" (consecutive-pivot comparison is the definition
//        of SMT); "realtime histogram stale" (intentional — VP is a
//        bar-close construct, gated since v1.5); "POC-trail polyline
//        per-tick churn" (vpShouldRedraw gate already prevents per-tick
//        redraw); "first historical session uninitialised" (section 3's
//        `na(vpSessHigh)` clause initialises bar 0); "orphan size arrays
//        desync" (vol and sent orphan pairs are independent, each
//        internally consistent); "AVWAP NaN from na hlc3" (chart-symbol
//        OHLC is never na — bars exist iff they have prices; the real na
//        risk, volume, is already nz()-guarded); "drawings leak on input
//        toggle" (Pine restarts the script on input change, clearing all
//        drawings); request.security for disabled symbols (Pine forbids
//        conditional request.security — not fixable, 3 of 40-call budget).
//        NOTED, not fixed — historical VP histograms: section 5 (redraw)
//        is gated by barstate.islast, so on a fresh load only the
//        developing session shows a histogram; completed sessions are
//        retained going forward as realtime sessions finish. Drawing all
//        historical sessions would blow the 500-box budget regardless
//        (one session = up to 80 boxes). A proper fix is a feature-scale
//        redraw redesign, out of scope for a bug-fix release.
// v3.4 — Two real fixes from a review (one review claim rejected).
//        Fix 1 — prev-session confluence indexed by [barOffset].
//        `checkConfluence` indexed currDev (v2.7) and composite (v3.0)
//        levels by [barOffset] to read them as of the pivot bar, but
//        the prev-session POC/VAH/VAL/sentiment were still read as
//        CURRENT values. A pivot in the last `pivotRightLen` bars of a
//        session confirms AFTER the session boundary — by which point
//        `prevSessPOC` has already advanced to the just-finalized
//        session. So a near-boundary pivot was tagged against the wrong
//        "previous" session. Now `prevSessPOC[barOffset]` etc. — the
//        prev-session levels as they stood at the pivot bar. `levelsInBar`
//        updated identically (iceberg passes barOffset=0 so no behaviour
//        change there, just symmetry).
//        Fix 2 — developing POC/VAH/VAL lines no longer orphaned at
//        session reset. Section 3 was setting `vpPocLine/VahLine/ValLine`
//        and the five VP labels to `na` WITHOUT deleting the underlying
//        objects. With extend.right the orphaned developing-POC line
//        stayed on-chart and overlapped the prevPocLine that section 1
//        draws for the SAME session's finalized POC — visual duplication,
//        plus one stale line/label set leaked per session, slowly eating
//        the 500 line/label budget. HVN lines / heatmap boxes / bin
//        labels right above were already deleted properly — the
//        POC/VAH/VAL lines were just the missed case. Now deleted before
//        the refs are nulled.
//        Rejected claim — "SMT samples cmp highs/lows at the chart pivot
//        bar instead of detecting confirmed pivots on the cmp symbols."
//        That is not a bug, it is the STANDARD definition of SMT
//        divergence: correlated assets are compared AT the chart's swing
//        point. Sampling cmp.high/low at the chart pivot bar is exactly
//        right. Detecting independent pivots per symbol and matching them
//        temporally is a different (and noisier) technique, not SMT.
// v3.3 — Split pivot length into independent Left / Right bar counts to
//        cut SMT divergence signal lag.
//        Problem: SMT used `ta.pivothigh(src, pivotLen, pivotLen)` — the
//        same value for both the left (significance) and right
//        (confirmation) sides. A pivot can't be confirmed until `right`
//        bars have closed without exceeding it — so pivotLen=5 meant
//        every SMT divergence printed 5 bars LATE. But the left side
//        adds no lag at all (those bars are already history when the
//        pivot bar prints) — only the right side does.
//        Fix: `pivotLen` → `pivotLeftLen` (default 5) + `pivotRightLen`
//        (default 3). Left keeps swing-significance strict; Right is
//        lowered to confirm faster. SMT signals now print 3 bars after
//        the pivot instead of 5 — a 40% lag cut — with the left-side
//        quality filter fully intact. Tradeoff: a smaller Right admits
//        more false pivots (a swing confirmed too early can still be
//        exceeded later); 2-3 is the sweet spot, 1 is too noisy.
//        All offset sites repointed from `pivotLen` to `pivotRightLen`:
//        the pivot bar is `pivotRightLen` bars back at confirmation, so
//        cmp-symbol sampling (`s1High[pivotRightLen]` etc.), the
//        confluence `barOffset`, `drawDivergence`'s `curBar`, and the
//        pivot-marker `plotshape` offsets all use pivotRightLen.
//        MIGRATION NOTE: the input rename resets saved pivot settings to
//        defaults (Left=5, Right=3). Users who ran pivotLen=N should set
//        Left=N and pick a Right (try 3, or N for identical old
//        behaviour). Symmetric Left==Right reproduces pre-v3.3 exactly.
// v3.2 — Revert v2.9: hoist `levelsInBar` call back to top-level.
//        v2.9 moved the iceberg `levelsInBar(low, high, 0)` call inside
//        the `if isBullIce or isBearIce` conditional on the reasoning
//        that:
//          (a) levelsInBar is a pure function — output unaffected by
//              call frequency, and
//          (b) Pine's "may develop gaps in internal series history"
//              warning wouldn't fire for pure functions.
//        Half right. Output IS unchanged in either placement (verified
//        — output values are pure functions of the global series Pine
//        maintains regardless of call frequency). But Pine v6's static
//        analyzer emits the warning for ANY user-defined function that
//        reads historical series via [barOffset] when called
//        conditionally — pure or not. The warning isn't a correctness
//        signal, it's a style/conservatism flag.
//        Net: v2.9 traded a clean editor for a microscopic per-bar
//        perf gain (~15 string-concat ops at most when no iceberg
//        fires). Not worth the user-visible warning. Hoisting back
//        restores warning-free compilation. Matches the
//        smtBearConf/smtBullConf top-level pattern.
//        No other code changes in this release.
// v3.1 — Two real fixes from the v3.0 review (rest of the review pushed back):
//        • Composite line left anchor. v3.0 drew composite POC/VAH/VAL
//          from `prevSessEndBar` (= bar_index - 1) — a 1-bar stub that
//          `extend.right` then carried forward. Visually inconsistent
//          with the prev-session lines (which span their full session).
//          Fix: track each contributing session's start bar in a new
//          `compositeSessionStartBars` array (parallel to highs/lows),
//          trim in lock-step, and anchor the composite line at the
//          OLDEST tracked session's start. Composite lines now visibly
//          span every session that contributed to the aggregate, then
//          extend right — same anchor pattern as prev-session lines.
//        • cPOC/cVAH/cVAL double-firing with pPOC/pVAH/pVAL during
//          composite warmup. When only one session is in the composite
//          (first finalize after script load), composite == prev
//          session by construction — firing both tags counted the
//          same level twice and inflated the ★N strength count.
//          Fix: gate the c-tags on `compositeSessionCount >= 2`. New
//          `var int compositeSessionCount` is series-tracked (updated
//          at each finalize), so `[barOffset]` indexing returns the
//          historical count at the pivot bar — symmetric with how
//          `compositePOC[barOffset]` etc. already work.
//        Items deliberately NOT changed (review claims rejected after
//        analysis):
//          - "computeProfile empty-bin infinite walk" — terminates in
//            ≤ rows iterations; bound is `(vaL > 0 or vaH < rows - 1)`.
//          - "matrix.get O(N·R²)" — actually called inside the j-loop,
//            not the k-loop. Total = N·R = 1600 worst case. Non-issue.
//          - "compositePOC[barOffset] cross-boundary semantics" — the
//            current behavior is correct (evaluate pivot against the
//            composite as it stood at the pivot bar's time).
//          - "Dashboard position-change not recreating table" — Pine
//            restarts the script on input change; `var table` resets
//            to `na`, triggering recreation with the new position.
//          - "countConfluenceTags double-space inflation" — current
//            code can't produce double-spaces; defensive fix not
//            currently needed.
// v3.0 — Composite (multi-session) Volume Profile + confluence refinements.
//        ── Main feature: Composite VP. ──
//        Aggregates the last N completed sessions into a single profile on
//        a unified price grid. Yields composite POC/VAH/VAL — an HTF
//        "where the cluster of attention is" reference, distinct from:
//          • prev-session levels (only the most recent session)
//          • naked POCs (individual untested POCs, no aggregation)
//        Each completed session's vpBins array is snapshotted into a
//        rolling matrix (max N rows). On every session finalize the matrix
//        is re-aggregated onto a fresh unified grid spanning all tracked
//        sessions' ranges, with overlap-ratio bin distribution to preserve
//        accuracy across mismatched session ranges. Cost is O(N × rows²)
//        per session-finalize (≤ 128k ops at upper limits) — well within
//        Pine's loop budget since recompute happens once per session.
//        Confluence: SMT pivots and icebergs at composite levels now tag
//        as `cPOC` / `cVAH` / `cVAL`, distinct from `POC`/`VAH`/`VAL`
//        (current) and `pPOC`/`pVAH`/`pVAL` (immediately-prior).
//        Dashboard: three new rows (Comp POC / Comp VAH / Comp VAL)
//        inserted after Prev VAL. Row count 21 → 24.
//        Drawing: composite POC drawn solid thick gold (default), VAH/VAL
//        dashed blue. Anchored at the most-recent session end with
//        extend.right — sits alongside prev-session lines on the chart.
//
//        ── Confluence system refinements: ──
//        • Confluence STRENGTH count surfaced. Was: ★ (binary). Now: ★N
//          where N = number of tag words in the confluence string.
//          A pivot tagged "POC pPOC(Bull) AVWAP +1.0σ" displays as ★4
//          instead of ★. Differentiates strong-confluence pivots from
//          single-tag ones at a glance on label + dashboard + alert.
//        • Naked-POC iteration no longer breaks on first match. A pivot
//          between two nPOCs (e.g., 1.33995 + 1.34005 with confTicks=10)
//          now tags BOTH. Same fix in `levelsInBar`.
// v2.9 — Iceberg confluence string moved inside the conditional. v2.8's
//        rejection of this fix was overcautious. The reasoning was: "Pine
//        v6 warns about conditional historical-series access". True in
//        general — but that warning applies to functions whose OWN
//        internal state depends on cumulative history (calling ta.*,
//        holding var arrays, etc.). `levelsInBar` is a pure read function:
//        no var, no ta.* calls — it only reads global series via
//        [barOffset] and builds a string. The global series Pine
//        maintains are unaffected by `levelsInBar`'s call frequency, so
//        calling it only on iceberg-firing bars produces identical
//        output. The hoist was a real concern for the smtBearConf /
//        smtBullConf pre-computes (which `checkConfluence` also reads
//        globals from but those happen to early-return on `na(price)`
//        so the cost is minimal anyway) — but for `iceConfluence` low/
//        high are never na on confirmed bars, so the full body was
//        running every bar. Now skipped on the 99%+ of bars where no
//        iceberg fires. Worst case if Pine v6 still emits a cosmetic
//        warning: yellow squiggle in editor; output remains correct.
//        Credit: user pushed back on v2.8's rejection — "the warning
//        doesn't create any incorrect value right?" Correct call.
// v2.8 — Post-v2.7 polish (carry-forward items flagged by code review):
//        • Header line 1 was still '[v2.6]'. v2.7 bumped the indicator()
//          declaration and the dashboard version cell but missed the
//          file-header comment — pure cosmetic, now in sync.
//        • Dashboard now includes a ±3σ row (between ±2σ and Naked POCs).
//          Previously when `showSigma3` was enabled the σ3 bands plotted
//          on-chart but the dashboard only listed σ1 and σ2 — incomplete.
//          Row count bumped 20→21; rows 11 onward all shifted +1.
//        Deliberately NOT changed: the iceConfluence top-level
//        pre-compute (`string iceConfluence = levelsInBar(low, high, 0)`).
//        Review suggested moving it inside `if isBullIce or isBearIce`
//        to skip the per-bar string work. Rejected — `levelsInBar`
//        reads `avwap[barOffset]`, `avwapSigma[barOffset]`, and (post
//        v2.7) `currDevPOC[barOffset]` etc. Calling it conditionally
//        re-introduces the very Pine v6 "may develop gaps in its
//        internal series history" warning the v1.5 hoist was designed
//        to avoid. The smtBearConf / smtBullConf pre-computes use the
//        identical pattern for the same reason. Per-bar string concat
//        cost is microscopic; Pine consistency wins.
// v2.7 — Historical-bar SMT confluence on currDev levels — actually works
//        this time. v2.6 PUBLISHED `currDevPOC/VAH/VAL` from section 4 on
//        every confirmed bar (correct), but missed that `checkConfluence`
//        was reading those vars without historical indexing. The SMT block
//        evaluates at the TOP of each bar, BEFORE section 4 publishes the
//        new currDev values — so at confirmation bar B, `currDevPOC` (no
//        index) returns end-of-bar-(B-1)'s value. The actual pivot fired
//        at bar B-pivotLen. The `pivotLen-1` bars of POC drift between
//        those two sample points silently masked legitimate confluence.
//        Fix: `checkConfluence` now reads `currDevPOC[barOffset]` /
//        `currDevVAH[barOffset]` / `currDevVAL[barOffset]` — the
//        developing levels as of the actual pivot bar. AVWAP/σ already
//        used `[barOffset]` indexing, this just extends the same pattern.
//        `levelsInBar` updated identically for symmetry (iceberg passes
//        barOffset=0, so [0]==no-index — zero behaviour change for the
//        iceberg call site, but the function is now consistent).
//        Visible impact: SMT pivots that printed near the developing POC/
//        VAH/VAL at the time of the pivot now get the ★ marker on both
//        the chart label and the dashboard's "Last Bull/Bear SMT" row.
// v2.6 — SMT confluence on historical bars actually works now:
//        v2.5 added the currDev check to `checkConfluence` but missed the
//        timing issue: `currDevPOC/VAH/VAL` were only set inside the redraw
//        block (gated by `barstate.islast`), so on historical bars they
//        stayed `na`. The new check `not na(currDevPOC) and ...` silently
//        evaluated false for every historical SMT pivot.
//        Fix: publish `currDevPOC/VAH/VAL` from section 4 (`barstate.is
//        confirmed`) so they're current on every closed bar — historical
//        and realtime. Now SMT pivots in the chart's history that sat on
//        the developing POC at THAT bar's time will correctly show ★.
//        (Redraw block still computes them too for its own drawing — same
//        values, minor duplication for code clarity.)
// v2.5 — SMT confluence gap fixed:
//        • `checkConfluence` (used by SMT pivot evaluation) now also checks
//          the CURRENT developing-session POC/VAH/VAL levels. Previously
//          only `levelsInBar` (used by iceberg) checked these — which is
//          why an iceberg sitting at the developing POC would get its
//          confluence ★, but an SMT pivot at the same price would not.
//          Long-standing gap from v2.0 when currDev levels were added to
//          iceberg confluence but not mirrored into SMT. Now consistent.
//        • Visible impact: SMT pivots that print near the current session's
//          POC/VAH/VAL now get the ★ marker on chart and in alert messages.
//          Renamed local helpers `atVAH`/`atVAL` → `atPVAH`/`atPVAL` to make
//          it clear those refer to PREVIOUS-session edges (distinct from
//          the new VAH/VAL current-session checks above them).
// v2.4 — SMT chart-label improvements:
//        • Multi-symbol divergence at the same pivot no longer stacks
//          invisibly. Previously when both (e.g.) EURUSD and AUDUSD
//          diverged against the same chart pivot, two lines AND two labels
//          were drawn at IDENTICAL coordinates — only the last one was
//          visible, the first was hidden underneath. Visualization now
//          matches the alert dedup behavior added in v1.5: ONE combined
//          line + label per pivot listing all diverging symbols.
//        • Confluence ★ marker now appears on the chart label itself, not
//          just in the dashboard's "last" row and alert messages. Tooltip
//          on the label also lists the specific confluence tags
//          (e.g., "pPOC(Bull) AVWAP +1.0σ") for the diverging pivot.
//        • drawDivergence signature changed: now takes a single `symList`
//          string plus `hasConf` and `confluenceStr` params instead of
//          per-symbol cmp values. Tooltip semantics unchanged otherwise.
// v2.3 — Drawing-budget hardening for v2.2's heavier visual mode:
//        • CRITICAL — orphaned histogram boxes (vpBoxes + vpSentBoxes) now
//          have a user-controlled cap. Each session's box count is tracked
//          in `orphanedVolSizes` / `orphanedSentSizes` arrays at session
//          reset; once `vpMaxOrphanSessions` is exceeded, the OLDEST whole
//          session's boxes are deleted FIFO. Predictable history depth
//          instead of letting Pine silently FIFO-drop random drawings when
//          the 500-box budget hits.
//          Default vpMaxOrphanSessions = 5 (gives ~120-160 orphaned boxes
//          at default vpRows=24, ~400-800 at vpRows=80 with Twin enabled).
//          Set to 0 to disable orphaning entirely (chart stays clean).
//        • Input tooltips on `vpHeatmap`, `vpHVNStyle`, and `vpGradientBins`
//          now explain budget implications and the pre-transparent base
//          color interaction with the gradient.
//        • No behaviour change at default settings — only matters when
//          multiple heavy visual features are enabled simultaneously.
// v2.2 — LuxAlgo-inspired visualization round 2 (all opt-in, defaults off):
//        • Gradient Bin Intensity. Bins fade with lower volume and saturate
//          at POC. Layered over the existing sentiment/VA hue using
//          color.from_gradient(LpM, 0, 1, faint, solid). Gives an at-a-glance
//          sense of which bins are heavyweights without changing color.
//        • Heatmap Overlay. Color each bin row across the FULL session
//          range, overlaid on the chart. Lets you spot high-volume zones at
//          a glance without looking at the right-side histogram.
//        • Developing POC Trail. Polyline showing how the POC moved bar-by-
//          bar through the session. Drift up = buyers building value at
//          higher prices; drift down = sellers winning; stable = balanced
//          two-way auction. Per-bar POC computed in section 4 alongside the
//          bin update, stored as chart.point in `pocTrailPoints`, drawn as
//          a single polyline at the end of the redraw block.
//        • HVN/LVN Zone style. Existing thin-line markers can now optionally
//          render as full-width transparent boxes spanning the session.
//          LuxAlgo's "consolidation zones" look. Toggle via vpHVNStyle
//          input (Line vs Zone).
//        • Added `max_polylines_count = 50` to the indicator declaration —
//          polylines have their own per-script budget.
// v2.1 — Review follow-up. Performance fix for v2.0's bin recompute, plus
//        three real-but-narrow correctness fixes flagged by code review:
//        • CRITICAL — VP bin recompute is now incremental when the session
//          range is stable. v2.0 did a full `recomputeBinsFromRaw` on EVERY
//          confirmed bar, which is correct but O(N²·R) cumulatively across
//          a session. On extreme combos (Weekly+ anchor on M1 chart with
//          vpRows=80) late-session recomputes exceeded Pine's per-bar loop
//          budget (~200k iterations) and the indicator would crash.
//          Now: track `lastRecompHigh / lastRecompLow`. Full recompute only
//          when the session range actually expands (rare after the first
//          few bars); otherwise `accumulateCurrentBar` adds the current bar
//          incrementally in O(vpRows). Typical case is now O(N·R), same as
//          a naive incremental approach, while remaining drift-free.
//        • `levelsInBar` now checks the σ3 bands (only σ1/σ2 before). v1.9's
//          σ3 toggle was respected in `checkConfluence` but missed in
//          `levelsInBar`, so an iceberg sitting at ±3σ would not get the
//          confluence tag even though an SMT pivot at the same price would.
//        • Iceberg bull/bear classification is mutually exclusive at the
//          threshold = 0.5 edge case. Previously a doji bar (close exactly
//          at midpoint) would satisfy both `closeHigh` and `closeLow`, and
//          the code silently picked Bull. Now neither fires — a midpoint
//          close is genuinely ambiguous (no absorption side).
//        • `InVA` confluence tag no longer fires redundantly alongside
//          `pVAH` / `pVAL`. A price exactly at VAH used to produce both
//          tags; now `InVA` requires being strictly past both edges by more
//          than the tick tolerance.
// v2.0 — Correctness release. Three real bugs and two signal-quality gaps:
//        • SMT inverse-correlation SAMPLING fix. For Positive-correlated
//          comparison symbols we sample cmp.HIGH at chart pivot highs and
//          cmp.LOW at chart pivot lows — which captures cmp's matching pivot
//          value. For Inverse pairs (e.g., DXY vs EURUSD) the cmp pivots in
//          the OPPOSITE direction; the previous code still sampled the same
//          side as the chart pivot, so the divergence comparison was reading
//          off the wrong side of the cmp's bar. Now flips: inverse symbols
//          sample cmp.LOW at chart pivot HIGH and cmp.HIGH at chart pivot
//          LOW. Bull/Bear semantics unchanged; only the underlying sampled
//          values change, producing cleaner ICT-aligned divergence detection
//          on inverse pairs.
//        • VP bin drift eliminated. Bins were previously accumulated
//          incrementally as vpSessHigh/Low expanded — so volume deposited
//          early in the session (under a narrower range) referred to
//          different price levels than bins deposited later. POC and value
//          area drifted with the range. Replaced incremental accumulation
//          with `recomputeBinsFromRaw` (called on each confirmed bar and at
//          session finalization) — rebuilds bins from raw bar history using
//          the FINAL range. O(barsInSession × vpRows) per call but well
//          within Pine's compute budget; max_bars_back raised to 5000 to
//          cover long sessions.
//        • Naked-POC grace period off-by-one. The check was `> created + 1`
//          which is a 2-bar grace, but the documented intent was 1-bar.
//          Fixed to `> created` (skip only the creation bar itself).
//        • AVWAP confluence on session-boundary pivots was triggering
//          spuriously. On the first bar of a new session, AVWAP = hlc3 and
//          σ = 0 (single-bar VWAP), so any nearby price would falsely
//          "match" AVWAP. Added `pivSigma > 0` guard to both `checkConfluence`
//          and `levelsInBar` — skips AVWAP/σ confluence when the AVWAP
//          hasn't yet developed.
//        • Iceberg confluence now checks the developing-session POC/VAH/VAL
//          (`currDevPOC/VAH/VAL`) in addition to the previous-session
//          levels, naked POCs, and AVWAP/σ. An iceberg sitting at the
//          developing POC is a high-quality signal that was previously
//          silent in the confluence tag.
// v1.9 — Audit bug-fix release:
//        • Iceberg detection no longer self-dilutes its own threshold. The
//          volume SMA and ATR are now computed with a [1]-offset (trailing
//          20 / 14 bars EXCLUDING the current bar). Previously a 2× volume
//          spike raised its own SMA enough that the realised ratio came in
//          just under iceVolMult, causing real iceberg bars to be missed.
//          Same fix applied to ATR for consistency. Volume-ratio displayed
//          in the iceberg tooltip is now accurate too.
//        • HVN/LVN lines no longer extend right across session boundaries.
//          They are session-bound markers — extending them right (alongside
//          POC/VAH/VAL, the genuine forward-reference levels) was visually
//          polluting subsequent sessions. Now always extend.none.
//        • HVN/LVN lines and per-bin volume labels are DELETED on session
//          reset, not orphaned. Histogram boxes are still orphaned (they
//          anchor to the past session's right edge and serve as a historical
//          profile reference); HVN/LVN lines and per-bin labels would either
//          clutter the new session or eat into Pine's 500-label budget over
//          many sessions.
//        • Confluence strings are now right-trimmed (no trailing space).
//        • Sentiment histogram bins in Twin layout no longer round up to a
//          minimum 1-bar width — near-balanced bins are now visually quiet
//          instead of falsely displaying a thin neutral bar.
// v1.8 — Inverse correlation support for SMT divergence:
//        Previously the SMT logic implicitly assumed all comparison symbols
//        were POSITIVELY correlated with the chart (move together). For
//        inverse pairs (EURUSD vs DXY, SPY vs VIX, BTC vs gold, etc.) the
//        divergence condition is actually the OPPOSITE — they're expected to
//        move in opposite directions, so a divergence is when they move the
//        SAME direction.
//        • Per-symbol Positive/Inverse correlation dropdown added to each
//          comparison row. Each symbol can be configured independently.
//        • Divergence check now flips based on correlation: positive pairs
//          fire on opposite movement, inverse pairs fire on matching
//          movement, exactly as ICT defines SMT divergence on inverse pairs.
//        • Diverged-symbol list (used in alerts + dashboard) tags inverse
//          pairs with " (inv)" suffix so you can see at a glance which
//          correlation type triggered the signal.
// v1.7 — VP Visualization upgrade (LuxAlgo-style, signature pieces only):
//        • Twin Profile layout: optional side-by-side rendering — sentiment
//          histogram (BBP per bin, green/red) on the left and volume
//          histogram on the right. Each shares the same vertical price
//          range, anchored at the right edge of the latest bar. Single-mode
//          layout (overlay sentiment color on volume bins) remains default.
//        • Per-bin volume labels (optional). Each bin gets a small label
//          showing `{vol} ({%-of-session})` for analytical depth.
//        • Profile edge labels (optional, on by default). Profile High and
//          Profile Low labels at the session range extremes, with tooltips
//          carrying total volume, bar count, and range %.
//        • Tracked drawings expanded to include `vpSentBoxes`, `vpBinLabels`,
//          `vpHighLabel`, `vpLowLabel` — all cleaned up on session reset
//          and re-created on each redraw cycle.
//        • Deliberate skips (per analyst's recommendation): no heatmap, no
//          developing-POC polyline, no three-tier color gradient, no
//          fixed-range anchor mode, no LuxAlgo sentiment-zone marker.
// v1.6 — Sentiment Profile + Money Flow + HVN/LVN (LuxAlgo-inspired):
//        • Per-bin bull/bear split (Sentiment Profile). A parallel
//          `vpBinsBull` array tracks the bull-classified volume per bin;
//          bear = total − bull. Bins colored by net sign when enabled —
//          green for buyer-dominated, red for seller-dominated, neutral
//          otherwise. Two classification methods: bar polarity (close vs
//          open) or buying pressure (close position in bar range).
//        • Money Flow weighting toggle. When ON, bin weight is
//          `volume × overlap × bin-midprice` (dollar value transacted) vs
//          the default `volume × overlap` (share count). More meaningful
//          on instruments with wide price variation.
//        • HVN / LVN classification. High Volume Nodes (≥ threshold % of
//          POC) and Low Volume Nodes (≤ threshold %) drawn as horizontal
//          lines through the current session, identifying value zones and
//          thin "no-mans-land" pass-through levels respectively.
//        • Prev-session POC sentiment captured at finalization and surfaced
//          in confluence tags as `pPOC(Bull)` / `pPOC(Bear)` so a bearish
//          iceberg at a buyer-dominated prior POC reads as a sharper
//          divergence signal than one at a neutral level.
//        • Dashboard: session sentiment summary (Bull% / Bear%), HVN/LVN
//          counts, prev-POC dashboard cell tagged with sentiment.
//
// NOTE on icebergs: true iceberg detection needs Level 2 / order-book data,
// which Pine does not have. This implementation uses the standard candlestick
// proxy: high volume + narrow range + extreme close = absorption footprint.
// Best paired with VP/AVWAP confluence gating for high-quality signals.

//@version=6
indicator('SMT + VP + AVWAP + Ice [v3.6]', 'SMT+VP3.6', overlay = true, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500, max_bars_back = 5000, max_polylines_count = 50)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Constants
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GREEN = #089981
RED   = #F23645
GRAY  = #878b94
GOLD  = #FFC107
BLUE  = #2196F3
AMBER = #FF9800

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs — SMT
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpPivot = 'SMT — Pivot Detection'
// v3.3: pivot length split into independent Left and Right bar counts.
// LEFT  = how many bars BEFORE the swing it must exceed. A swing-quality
//         filter — higher = stricter. Adds ZERO signal lag (those bars are
//         already history when the pivot bar prints).
// RIGHT = how many bars AFTER the swing must fail to exceed it before the
//         pivot is confirmed. THIS is the entire SMT signal lag — a
//         divergence prints `pivotRightLen` bars after the actual pivot.
//         Lower = faster signal but more false pivots (a "swing" confirmed
//         too early can still be exceeded a few bars later). 2-3 is the
//         usual sweet spot; 1 is too noisy.
pivotLeftLen  = input.int(5, 'Pivot Left Bars',  minval = 1, maxval = 50, tooltip = 'Bars BEFORE a swing that it must exceed to count as a pivot. Swing-significance filter — higher is stricter. Costs NO signal delay (these bars are already history when the pivot prints).', group = grpPivot)
pivotRightLen = input.int(3, 'Pivot Right Bars', minval = 1, maxval = 50, tooltip = 'Bars AFTER a swing that must fail to exceed it before the pivot confirms. THIS is the SMT signal lag — a divergence prints this many bars after the pivot. Lower = faster but more false pivots. 2-3 is the usual sweet spot; 1 is too noisy.', group = grpPivot)
pivotSrcMode = input.string('Wick', 'Pivot Source', options = ['Wick', 'Body'], tooltip = 'Wick uses high/low; Body uses max/min of open/close.', group = grpPivot)
showPivotMarkers = input.bool(false, 'Show Pivot Markers', group = grpPivot)

grpSymbols = 'SMT — Comparison Symbols'
// Each symbol row: [enable checkbox] [symbol picker] [Positive/Inverse correlation].
// Positive: chart and comparison are expected to move TOGETHER (ES/NQ/YM, BTC/ETH).
// Inverse:  chart and comparison are expected to move OPPOSITE (EURUSD/DXY, SPY/VIX).
// Divergence logic flips automatically based on this setting.
sym1Enabled = input.bool(true,  '', inline = 's1', group = grpSymbols)
sym1        = input.symbol('CME_MINI:ES1!', 'Symbol 1', inline = 's1', group = grpSymbols)
sym1Corr    = input.string('Positive', '', options = ['Positive', 'Inverse'], inline = 's1', group = grpSymbols, tooltip = 'Positive: chart and symbol move together (ES vs NQ, BTC vs ETH). Inverse: chart and symbol move opposite (EURUSD vs DXY, SPY vs VIX). The divergence condition flips automatically for Inverse.')
sym2Enabled = input.bool(true,  '', inline = 's2', group = grpSymbols)
sym2        = input.symbol('CME_MINI:NQ1!', 'Symbol 2', inline = 's2', group = grpSymbols)
sym2Corr    = input.string('Positive', '', options = ['Positive', 'Inverse'], inline = 's2', group = grpSymbols)
sym3Enabled = input.bool(false, '', inline = 's3', group = grpSymbols)
sym3        = input.symbol('CBOT_MINI:YM1!', 'Symbol 3', inline = 's3', group = grpSymbols)
sym3Corr    = input.string('Positive', '', options = ['Positive', 'Inverse'], inline = 's3', group = grpSymbols)

grpStyle = 'SMT — Style'
bullColor   = input.color(GREEN, 'Bullish SMT', group = grpStyle)
bearColor   = input.color(RED,   'Bearish SMT', group = grpStyle)
lineWidth   = input.int(2, 'Line Width', minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = grpStyle)
lineStyleIn = input.string('Dashed', 'Line Style', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = grpStyle)
showLabel   = input.bool(true, 'Show Symbol Label', group = grpStyle)
labelSize   = input.string('small', 'Label Size', options = ['tiny', 'small', 'normal'], group = grpStyle)

grpAlerts = 'SMT — Alerts'
alertBull = input.bool(true, 'Alert on Bullish SMT', group = grpAlerts)
alertBear = input.bool(true, 'Alert on Bearish SMT', group = grpAlerts)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs — Volume Profile (Current + Previous Session)
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpVP = 'Volume Profile'
vpEnabled    = input.bool(true, 'Show Volume Profile', group = grpVP)
vpAnchorIn   = input.string('Daily', 'Anchor', options = ['Daily', 'Weekly', 'Monthly'], group = grpVP)
vpRows       = input.int(24, 'Profile Rows', minval = 5, maxval = 80, tooltip = 'More rows = finer resolution but more boxes.', group = grpVP)
vpValueAreaP = input.float(70.0, 'Value Area %', minval = 50, maxval = 95, step = 1, group = grpVP) / 100.0
vpShowHist   = input.bool(true, 'Show Histogram', group = grpVP)
vpHistWidth  = input.int(40, 'Histogram Width (bars)', minval = 5, maxval = 200, group = grpVP)
vpShowPOC    = input.bool(true, 'Show Current POC',    group = grpVP)
vpShowVA     = input.bool(true, 'Show Current VAH/VAL', group = grpVP)
vpShowLabels = input.bool(true, 'Show Price Labels', group = grpVP)
vpExtend     = input.bool(true, 'Extend Current Levels Right', group = grpVP)
vpPocColor   = input.color(GOLD, 'POC Color', group = grpVP)
vpVaColor    = input.color(BLUE, 'VAH/VAL Color', group = grpVP)
vpVaFill     = input.color(color.new(BLUE, 80), 'Value Area Fill', group = grpVP)
vpOutFill    = input.color(color.new(GRAY, 80), 'Outside VA Fill', group = grpVP)

grpPrev = 'Previous Session Levels'
vpShowPrev      = input.bool(true, 'Show Previous Session POC/VAH/VAL', group = grpPrev)
vpPrevPocColor  = input.color(color.new(GOLD, 20), 'Prev POC Color', group = grpPrev)
vpPrevVaColor   = input.color(color.new(BLUE, 20), 'Prev VAH/VAL Color', group = grpPrev)
vpPrevLineWidth = input.int(2, 'Prev POC Line Width', minval = 1, maxval = 4, group = grpPrev)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs — Composite / Multi-session Volume Profile (v3.0)
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Composite VP aggregates the last N completed sessions into a single
// profile on a unified price grid. Yields a "where attention clustered
// over multiple sessions" HTF reference — complements naked POCs
// (untested individuals) and prev-session levels (most recent only).
grpVPComp           = 'Composite Volume Profile'
vpCompositeEnabled  = input.bool(true, 'Show Composite Profile', tooltip = 'Aggregates last N completed sessions into a unified profile. Yields composite POC/VAH/VAL as HTF reference levels. Updates on every session finalize.', group = grpVPComp)
vpCompositeSessions = input.int(5, 'Sessions to Aggregate', minval = 2, maxval = 20, tooltip = 'Number of completed sessions to include. Higher = smoother HTF reference but slower to adapt to regime change. Recompute is O(N × rows) per session-finalize (v3.5 optimised the merge from O(N × rows²)) — cheap even at the maximum N=20, vpRows=80.', group = grpVPComp)
vpCompositePocColor = input.color(color.new(GOLD, 20), 'Composite POC Color', group = grpVPComp)
vpCompositeVaColor  = input.color(color.new(BLUE, 20), 'Composite VAH/VAL Color', group = grpVPComp)
vpCompositeWidth    = input.int(3, 'Composite POC Line Width', minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = grpVPComp)
vpShowCompositeLabels = input.bool(true, 'Show Composite Labels', group = grpVPComp)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs — Volume Profile Advanced (Money Flow, Sentiment, HVN/LVN)
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpVPAdv = 'VP Advanced — Sentiment & Money Flow'
vpSource          = input.string('Volume', 'Profile Source', options = ['Volume', 'Money Flow'], tooltip = 'Volume: bin = overlap × volume (share/contract count). Money Flow: bin = overlap × volume × bin-midprice (dollar value transacted). Money Flow gives a more meaningful picture on instruments with wide price variation (crypto, equities); for tight-range forex pairs the difference is small.', group = grpVPAdv)
vpSentiment       = input.bool(true, 'Color Bins by Sentiment (Bull/Bear)', tooltip = 'Splits each bin into bull vs bear volume; bin is colored green if buyers dominated at that price level, red if sellers did, gray if balanced. When OFF, bins use the standard inside-VA / outside-VA colors.', group = grpVPAdv)
vpSentimentMethod = input.string('Bar Polarity', 'Sentiment Method', options = ['Bar Polarity', 'Buying Pressure'], tooltip = 'Bar Polarity: bullish if close > open. Buying Pressure: bullish if (close-low) > (high-close), i.e. closed in upper half of bar range.', group = grpVPAdv)
vpBullBinColor    = input.color(color.new(GREEN, 60), 'Bullish Bin Color', group = grpVPAdv)
vpBearBinColor    = input.color(color.new(RED, 60), 'Bearish Bin Color', group = grpVPAdv)
vpNeutralBinColor = input.color(color.new(GRAY, 70), 'Neutral Bin Color', group = grpVPAdv)

grpHVN = 'HVN / LVN Classification'
vpShowHVN      = input.bool(false, 'Mark HVN / LVN Levels', tooltip = 'High Volume Nodes (HVN) = consolidation/value zones — price tends to dwell. Low Volume Nodes (LVN) = thin zones — price tends to traverse quickly, good no-mans-land for stop placement.', group = grpHVN)
vpHVNThreshold = input.float(0.7, 'HVN Threshold (% of POC)', minval = 0.3, maxval = 0.95, step = 0.05, tooltip = 'Bin counts as HVN if its volume is at least this fraction of the POC bin. 0.7 = 70%.', group = grpHVN)
vpLVNThreshold = input.float(0.2, 'LVN Threshold (% of POC)', minval = 0.05, maxval = 0.4, step = 0.05, tooltip = 'Bin counts as LVN if its volume is between 0 and this fraction of the POC bin. 0.2 = 20%.', group = grpHVN)
vpHVNColor     = input.color(color.new(GOLD, 50), 'HVN Line Color', group = grpHVN)
vpLVNColor     = input.color(color.new(GRAY, 60), 'LVN Line Color', group = grpHVN)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs — VP Visualization (Twin Layout, Bin Labels, Edge Labels)
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpVPViz = 'VP Visualization'
vpProfileLayout  = input.string('Single', 'Profile Layout', options = ['Single', 'Twin (Volume + Sentiment)'], tooltip = 'Single: one histogram with bins colored by sentiment or VA. Twin: separate sentiment histogram (closer to chart, width proportional to |Bull-Bear| per bin) and volume histogram (further right, width proportional to total volume).', group = grpVPViz)
vpShowBinLabels  = input.bool(false, 'Show Per-Bin Volume Labels', tooltip = 'Each histogram bin gets a small label showing its volume amount and % of session total. Adds visual density — use selectively.', group = grpVPViz)
vpShowEdgeLabels = input.bool(true, 'Show Profile High / Low Labels', tooltip = 'Mark the top and bottom of the session profile range with labels. Hover for total volume, bar count, range %.', group = grpVPViz)
vpTwinSentBull   = input.color(color.new(GREEN, 55), 'Twin: Bull Sentiment Color', group = grpVPViz)
vpTwinSentBear   = input.color(color.new(RED, 55),   'Twin: Bear Sentiment Color', group = grpVPViz)
vpTwinVolColor   = input.color(color.new(BLUE, 70),  'Twin: Volume Color', tooltip = 'In Twin layout the volume bins are color-neutral by default since sentiment is already shown on the other histogram.', group = grpVPViz)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs — VP Visualization Advanced (LuxAlgo-inspired enhancements)
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpVPViz2 = 'VP Visualization — Advanced'
vpGradientBins    = input.bool(false, 'Gradient Bin Intensity', tooltip = 'Bins fade with lower volume, saturate to the user-chosen bin color at POC. Layered over the existing sentiment/VA hue. NOTE: gradient saturation tops out at the transparency YOUR sentiment colors already have (default Bull = 60% transparent, so the POC bin will reach 60% transparent at most, not solid). For a more dramatic gradient set Bull/Bear color transparency lower (closer to 0).', group = grpVPViz2)
vpHeatmap         = input.bool(false, 'Heatmap Overlay (full session)', tooltip = 'Color each bin across the FULL session range, overlaid on the chart. Lets you spot high-volume price zones at a glance without looking at the right-side histogram. Heatmap boxes are deleted at session reset (not orphaned) to protect against budget overflow on multi-session charts. Enabling alongside Twin Layout + HVN Zones at vpRows >= 50 may need vpMaxOrphanSessions lowered.', group = grpVPViz2)
vpHeatmapOpacity  = input.int(85, 'Heatmap Opacity (lower = darker)', minval = 70, maxval = 95, group = grpVPViz2)
vpDevPocTrail     = input.bool(false, 'Developing POC Trail', tooltip = 'Polyline showing how the POC moved bar-by-bar through the session. Drifting up = buyers building value at higher prices. Drifting down = sellers. Stable = balanced two-way auction.', group = grpVPViz2)
vpDevPocColor     = input.color(GOLD, 'Dev POC Trail Color', group = grpVPViz2)
vpHVNStyle        = input.string('Line', 'HVN / LVN Style', options = ['Line', 'Zone'], tooltip = 'Line: thin horizontal markers (default, low budget). Zone: full-width boxes across the session for each HVN/LVN bin — LuxAlgo-style "consolidation zone" rendering, more visually prominent but consumes more of the box budget. Zone boxes are deleted at session reset.', group = grpVPViz2)
vpHVNZoneOpacity  = input.int(80, 'HVN Zone Opacity (lower = darker)', minval = 60, maxval = 95, group = grpVPViz2)
vpLVNZoneOpacity  = input.int(90, 'LVN Zone Opacity (lower = darker)', minval = 60, maxval = 95, group = grpVPViz2)
vpMaxOrphanSessions = input.int(5, 'Max Orphaned History Sessions', minval = 0, maxval = 30, tooltip = 'Histogram boxes from completed sessions are kept on-chart as historical profile reference. This caps how many past sessions to keep visible. Lower values = less chart clutter and protect against the 500-box budget when Twin/Heatmap/HVN-Zones are all enabled. Set to 0 to delete all histogram boxes on session reset (no historical reference).', group = grpVPViz2)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs — Naked POCs
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpNPOC = 'Naked POCs'
nPocEnabled = input.bool(true, 'Track Naked POCs', tooltip = 'Save each completed session POC; remove when price re-touches.', group = grpNPOC)
nPocMax     = input.int(20, 'Max Tracked', minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = grpNPOC)
nPocColor   = input.color(color.new(AMBER, 30), 'Color', group = grpNPOC)
nPocStyleIn = input.string('Dotted', 'Line Style', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = grpNPOC)
nPocLabels  = input.bool(true, 'Show Labels', group = grpNPOC)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs — Anchored VWAP + σ Bands
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpAvwap = 'Anchored VWAP'
avwapEnabled = input.bool(true, 'Show Anchored VWAP', tooltip = 'Session-anchored VWAP using the same anchor as Volume Profile.', group = grpAvwap)
avwapColor   = input.color(#FF6D00, 'AVWAP Color', group = grpAvwap)
avwapWidth   = input.int(2, 'AVWAP Line Width', minval = 1, maxval = 4, group = grpAvwap)

showSigma1  = input.bool(true,  '', inline = 'sg1', group = grpAvwap)
sigma1Mult  = input.float(1.0, '±σ #1 ×', minval = 0.1, maxval = 5, step = 0.1, inline = 'sg1', group = grpAvwap)
sigma1Color = input.color(color.new(#FF6D00, 40), '', inline = 'sg1', group = grpAvwap)

showSigma2  = input.bool(true,  '', inline = 'sg2', group = grpAvwap)
sigma2Mult  = input.float(2.0, '±σ #2 ×', minval = 0.1, maxval = 5, step = 0.1, inline = 'sg2', group = grpAvwap)
sigma2Color = input.color(color.new(#FF6D00, 60), '', inline = 'sg2', group = grpAvwap)

showSigma3  = input.bool(false, '', inline = 'sg3', group = grpAvwap)
sigma3Mult  = input.float(3.0, '±σ #3 ×', minval = 0.1, maxval = 5, step = 0.1, inline = 'sg3', group = grpAvwap)
sigma3Color = input.color(color.new(#FF6D00, 75), '', inline = 'sg3', group = grpAvwap)

fillBands    = input.bool(true, 'Fill Between Bands', group = grpAvwap)
fillOpacity  = input.int(92, 'Fill Opacity (lower = darker)', minval = 60, maxval = 99, group = grpAvwap)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs — Confluence
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpConf = 'Confluence'
confEnabled = input.bool(true, 'Detect Confluence at SMT', group = grpConf)
confTicks   = input.int(10, 'Distance (ticks)', minval = 1, maxval = 200, tooltip = 'SMT pivots within this many ticks of a VP/AVWAP level count as confluence.', group = grpConf)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs — Iceberg / Absorption
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpIce = 'Iceberg / Absorption'
iceEnabled        = input.bool(true, 'Detect Iceberg / Absorption', tooltip = 'Flags high-volume narrow-range bars that close at one extreme — a proxy for hidden iceberg-order absorption.', group = grpIce)
iceVolMult        = input.float(2.0, 'Volume Multiplier (× SMA20)', minval = 1.0, maxval = 10, step = 0.1, tooltip = 'Bar volume must exceed this multiple of the 20-bar volume SMA.', group = grpIce)
iceRangeMult      = input.float(0.5, 'Max Range (× ATR14)', minval = 0.1, maxval = 2.0, step = 0.05, tooltip = 'Bar range must be LESS than this multiple of ATR(14). Narrow range = absorption.', group = grpIce)
iceCloseThreshold = input.float(0.33, 'Close Position Threshold', minval = 0.1, maxval = 0.5, step = 0.05, tooltip = 'Close must be in top/bottom N of bar range. 0.33 = top/bottom third.', group = grpIce)
iceRequireConf    = input.bool(true, 'Require VP/AVWAP Confluence', tooltip = 'Only fire icebergs whose bar range straddles a tracked level.', group = grpIce)
iceAlertEnabled   = input.bool(true, 'Alert on Iceberg', group = grpIce)
iceBullColor      = input.color(GREEN, 'Bullish Iceberg', group = grpIce)
iceBearColor      = input.color(RED,   'Bearish Iceberg', group = grpIce)
iceMarkerSize     = input.string('small', 'Marker Size', options = ['tiny', 'small', 'normal'], group = grpIce)
iceMarkerText     = input.string('🧊', 'Marker Text', tooltip = 'Falls back to text if emoji does not render on your platform.', group = grpIce)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs — Dashboard
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpDash = 'Dashboard'
showDash = input.bool(true, 'Show Dashboard', group = grpDash)
dashPos  = input.string('Top Right', 'Position', options = ['Top Right', 'Top Left', 'Bottom Right', 'Bottom Left', 'Middle Right'], group = grpDash)
dashSize = input.string('small', 'Text Size', options = ['tiny', 'small', 'normal'], group = grpDash)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Helpers
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
getLineStyle(string s) =>
    switch s
        'Solid'  => line.style_solid
        'Dashed' => line.style_dashed
        'Dotted' => line.style_dotted
        =>          line.style_dashed

getLabelSize(string s) =>
    switch s
        'tiny'   => size.tiny
        'small'  => size.small
        'normal' => size.normal
        =>          size.small

getDashPosition(string s) =>
    switch s
        'Top Left'      => position.top_left
        'Top Right'     => position.top_right
        'Bottom Left'   => position.bottom_left
        'Bottom Right'  => position.bottom_right
        'Middle Right'  => position.middle_right
        =>                 position.top_right

shortName(string s) =>
    int colonIdx = str.pos(s, ':')
    na(colonIdx) ? s : str.substring(s, colonIdx + 1)

// v3.6: clamp a bar-index x-coordinate for line/box drawing. Pine throws
// runtime error RE10026 ("bar index ... is too far from the current bar
// index") when an xloc.bar_index drawing coordinate sits more than
// ~max_bars_back bars before the current bar. On a 1-minute chart a VP
// session, the composite multi-session span, or an unusually long first
// session can exceed that window — the error never appears on higher
// timeframes because their sessions hold far fewer bars.
// Every drawing this is applied to either uses extend.right or is a
// horizontal level reference, so clamping the LEFT anchor only shortens
// the drawn segment slightly — the price level it represents is unchanged.
safeLeftBar(int b) => na(b) ? bar_index : math.max(b, bar_index - 4900)

pivotSrcHigh = pivotSrcMode == 'Body' ? math.max(open, close) : high
pivotSrcLow  = pivotSrcMode == 'Body' ? math.min(open, close) : low

// Session boundary detection — used by both Volume Profile and Anchored VWAP.
vpAnchorTF = vpAnchorIn == 'Daily' ? 'D' : vpAnchorIn == 'Weekly' ? 'W' : 'M'
isNewVPSession = ta.change(time(vpAnchorTF)) != 0

// Profile computation — returns POC bin index, value-area bin indices, total volume.
computeProfile(array<float> bins, int rows, float vaTargetRatio) =>
    int   pocIdx = 0
    float maxV   = 0.0
    float totalV = 0.0
    for i = 0 to rows - 1
        float v = array.get(bins, i)
        totalV += v
        if v > maxV
            maxV   := v
            pocIdx := i
    int   vaL = pocIdx
    int   vaH = pocIdx
    float vaV = array.get(bins, pocIdx)
    float target = totalV * vaTargetRatio
    while vaV < target and (vaL > 0 or vaH < rows - 1)
        float upV = vaH < rows - 1 ? array.get(bins, vaH + 1) : -1.0
        float dnV = vaL > 0        ? array.get(bins, vaL - 1) : -1.0
        if upV < 0 and dnV < 0
            break
        if upV >= dnV
            vaH += 1
            vaV += upV
        else
            vaL -= 1
            vaV += dnV
    [pocIdx, vaL, vaH, totalV]


//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// COMPARISON SYMBOL DATA + PIVOTS (must run on every bar before SMT block)
//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
[s1High, s1Low] = request.security(sym1, timeframe.period, [pivotSrcHigh, pivotSrcLow], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
[s2High, s2Low] = request.security(sym2, timeframe.period, [pivotSrcHigh, pivotSrcLow], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
[s3High, s3Low] = request.security(sym3, timeframe.period, [pivotSrcHigh, pivotSrcLow], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

// v3.3: asymmetric L/R — pivotRightLen controls confirmation lag.
phVal = ta.pivothigh(pivotSrcHigh, pivotLeftLen, pivotRightLen)
plVal = ta.pivotlow (pivotSrcLow,  pivotLeftLen, pivotRightLen)

//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ANCHORED VWAP + σ BANDS
//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Session-anchored VWAP. Confirmed-bar accumulation gives exact historical
// values; the realtime bar adds a live projection on top so the displayed
// VWAP is up-to-date instead of one bar stale.
//
// σ formula:  variance = Σ(P²·V)/ΣV − VWAP²    (O(1) per bar, no growing array)

var float cumPV   = 0.0   // Σ(typical price · volume)
var float cumV    = 0.0   // Σ(volume)
var float cumPV2  = 0.0   // Σ(typical² · volume)

// Confirmed-bar accumulation. On a session boundary, reset to this bar only.
// nz(volume) — some feeds (OANDA forex, certain index feeds) report `na`
// volume on individual bars. Without nz(), a single na bar poisons the whole
// cumulative sum via NaN propagation and AVWAP becomes na forever.
if avwapEnabled and barstate.isconfirmed
    float tp = hlc3
    float vol = nz(volume)
    float pv = tp * vol
    if isNewVPSession or cumV == 0
        cumPV  := pv
        cumV   := vol
        cumPV2 := tp * pv
    else
        cumPV  += pv
        cumV   += vol
        cumPV2 += tp * pv

// Live projection — for the realtime bar before close, add the running
// hlc3·volume on top of the confirmed accumulation so the AVWAP displayed
// includes the current tick.
float liveCumPV  = cumPV
float liveCumV   = cumV
float liveCumPV2 = cumPV2
if avwapEnabled and not barstate.isconfirmed
    float tp = hlc3
    float vol = nz(volume)
    float pv = tp * vol
    if isNewVPSession or cumV == 0
        liveCumPV  := pv
        liveCumV   := vol
        liveCumPV2 := tp * pv
    else
        liveCumPV  := cumPV  + pv
        liveCumV   := cumV   + vol
        liveCumPV2 := cumPV2 + tp * pv

float avwap      = avwapEnabled and liveCumV > 0 ? liveCumPV / liveCumV : na
float avwapVar   = avwapEnabled and liveCumV > 0 ? math.max(0.0, liveCumPV2 / liveCumV - avwap * avwap) : na
float avwapSigma = na(avwapVar) ? na : math.sqrt(avwapVar)

float avwapU1 = na(avwap) or na(avwapSigma) ? na : avwap + sigma1Mult * avwapSigma
float avwapL1 = na(avwap) or na(avwapSigma) ? na : avwap - sigma1Mult * avwapSigma
float avwapU2 = na(avwap) or na(avwapSigma) ? na : avwap + sigma2Mult * avwapSigma
float avwapL2 = na(avwap) or na(avwapSigma) ? na : avwap - sigma2Mult * avwapSigma
float avwapU3 = na(avwap) or na(avwapSigma) ? na : avwap + sigma3Mult * avwapSigma
float avwapL3 = na(avwap) or na(avwapSigma) ? na : avwap - sigma3Mult * avwapSigma

//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// STATE
//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// SMT state — previous-pivot snapshots, used to evaluate consecutive divergences.
var float prevPHChart = na
var float prevPHS1    = na
var float prevPHS2    = na
var float prevPHS3    = na
var int   prevPHBar   = na

var float prevPLChart = na
var float prevPLS1    = na
var float prevPLS2    = na
var float prevPLS3    = na
var int   prevPLBar   = na

// Last-fired SMT event for the dashboard.
var int    lastBullBar = na
var string lastBullSym = ''
var float  lastBullPrice = na
var bool   lastBullConf = false
var int    lastBullConfCount = 0     // v3.0: confluence tag count for ★N display
var int    lastBearBar = na
var string lastBearSym = ''
var float  lastBearPrice = na
var bool   lastBearConf = false
var int    lastBearConfCount = 0     // v3.0

// Iceberg tracking — session count + last event.
var int    iceCount    = 0
var int    lastIceBar  = na
var string lastIceType = ''   // 'Bull' or 'Bear'
var bool   lastIceConf = false
var int    lastIceConfCount = 0      // v3.0

// VP session aggregates.
var float vpSessHigh  = na
var float vpSessLow   = na
var int   vpSessStart = na
var array<float> vpBins     = array.new<float>(vpRows, 0.0)   // total volume per bin
var array<float> vpBinsBull = array.new<float>(vpRows, 0.0)   // bull-classified volume per bin; bear = vpBins - vpBinsBull

// VP developing-session drawings.
var array<box>   vpBoxes        = array.new<box>()     // volume histogram bins
var array<box>   vpSentBoxes    = array.new<box>()     // sentiment histogram bins (twin layout only)
var array<line>  vpHVNLines     = array.new<line>()    // HVN/LVN markers — Line style
var array<box>   vpHVNZoneBoxes = array.new<box>()     // HVN/LVN markers — Zone style (full-width boxes)
var array<box>   vpHeatmapBoxes = array.new<box>()     // heatmap overlay boxes (full-session per-bin)
var array<label> vpBinLabels    = array.new<label>()   // per-bin volume labels (toggle)
var array<chart.point> pocTrailPoints = array.new<chart.point>()   // developing POC trail (per-bar POC prices)
var polyline pocTrailPolyline = na

// Orphaned-histogram tracking. Each completed session's volume + sentiment
// histogram boxes get moved into these arrays at session reset so they
// remain on-chart as historical profile reference. Parallel "sizes" arrays
// track how many boxes each session contributed so we can evict whole
// sessions FIFO when vpMaxOrphanSessions is exceeded — keeps the chart
// from silently dropping random drawings when Pine's 500-box budget hits.
var array<box> orphanedVpBoxes      = array.new<box>()
var array<box> orphanedVpSentBoxes  = array.new<box>()
var array<int> orphanedVolSizes     = array.new<int>()
var array<int> orphanedSentSizes    = array.new<int>()
var line  vpPocLine   = na
var line  vpVahLine   = na
var line  vpValLine   = na
var label vpPocLabel  = na
var label vpVahLabel  = na
var label vpValLabel  = na
var label vpHighLabel = na   // profile high edge label
var label vpLowLabel  = na   // profile low edge label

// Cached current developing levels (for confluence + dashboard).
var float currDevPOC = na
var float currDevVAH = na
var float currDevVAL = na

// HVN/LVN counts (for dashboard).
var int hvnCount = 0
var int lvnCount = 0

// State for the incremental-vs-recompute decision. We only do a full
// `recomputeBinsFromRaw` when the session range has actually expanded since
// the last recompute. While the range is stable, each confirmed bar just
// adds its volume into the existing (already-correctly-aligned) bins. This
// turns the worst case from O(N²·R) per session down to O(N·R) for typical
// sessions where the range stabilizes after the first few bars.
var float lastRecompHigh = na
var float lastRecompLow  = na

// Per-session bar counter — used in the profile edge-label tooltip so the user
// can see how many bars are aggregated into the developing profile.
var int vpSessBarCount = 0

// Tracks the last bar on which the VP histogram was redrawn so we don't
// delete-and-rebuild ~24 boxes on every realtime tick when nothing changed.
var int lastVpDrawBar = na

// Previous session finalized levels.
var float  prevSessPOC = na
var float  prevSessVAH = na
var float  prevSessVAL = na
var int    prevSessStartBar = na
var int    prevSessEndBar   = na
var string prevSessPOCSentiment = na   // 'Bull' / 'Bear' / 'Neutral' — used to enrich confluence tags
var line   prevPocLine  = na
var line   prevVahLine  = na
var line   prevValLine  = na
var label  prevPocLabel = na
var label  prevVahLabel = na
var label  prevValLabel = na

// Composite VP — last N completed sessions aggregated into a unified
// profile (v3.0). Each completed session's vpBins is snapshotted as a row
// of `compositeSessionBins`; per-session high/low/start-bar stored in
// parallel arrays so the merge step can distribute bins onto the unified
// composite grid via overlap ratios, and the chart line can anchor at
// the OLDEST contributing session's start (v3.1 fix — was anchoring at
// prevSessEndBar = 1 bar before current, producing a tiny stub before
// extend.right kicked in).
// `compositeSessionCount` is the historical series of the row count —
// used by checkConfluence/levelsInBar to gate cPOC/cVAH/cVAL tags so they
// don't double-fire alongside pPOC/pVAH/pVAL during the N<2 warmup
// period when composite IS the prev session (v3.1 fix).
var matrix<float> compositeSessionBins = matrix.new<float>(0, vpRows, 0.0)
var array<float>  compositeSessionHighs     = array.new<float>()
var array<float>  compositeSessionLows      = array.new<float>()
var array<int>    compositeSessionStartBars = array.new<int>()
var array<float>  compositeBins             = array.new<float>(vpRows, 0.0)
var int   compositeSessionCount = 0
var float compositePOC       = na
var float compositeVAH       = na
var float compositeVAL       = na
var float compositeRangeHigh = na
var float compositeRangeLow  = na
var line   compositePocLine  = na
var line   compositeVahLine  = na
var line   compositeValLine  = na
var label  compositePocLabel = na
var label  compositeVahLabel = na
var label  compositeValLabel = na

// Naked POC tracking — each entry is a session-finalized POC that hasn't been
// re-touched yet. Parallel arrays for price, creation bar (= the bar where the
// POC was pushed, used for the 1-bar grace period in the touch check), line,
// and label.
var array<float> nakedPOCs            = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   nakedPOCCreationBars = array.new<int>()
var array<line>  nakedPOCLines        = array.new<line>()
var array<label> nakedPOCLabels       = array.new<label>()

// Dashboard table.
var table dashTable = na

// Style derivations.
lineStyle  = getLineStyle(lineStyleIn)
nPocStyle  = getLineStyle(nPocStyleIn)
lblSize    = getLabelSize(labelSize)
dashTxtSz  = getLabelSize(dashSize)

//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// HELPERS — drift-free VP recomputation
//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Recompute vpBins / vpBinsBull from raw bar history using the CURRENT
// vpSessHigh / vpSessLow as the bin range. Required because vpSessHigh/Low
// expand during the session — under incremental accumulation, bins assigned
// in early bars would refer to different price ranges than bins assigned
// later. Recomputing from raw on each redraw eliminates this drift.
//
// Must be defined AFTER the STATE section because it references the global
// `vpBins` / `vpBinsBull` arrays and the `vpSessHigh` / `vpSessLow` /
// `vpSessStart` / `vpRows` / `vpSource` / `vpSentimentMethod` symbols. Pine
// does not forward-resolve function-body identifiers.
//
// startOffset = 0 → include the current bar (developing redraw)
// startOffset = 1 → exclude the current bar (used at session finalization,
//                   where the current bar is the first bar of the NEW session
//                   and shouldn't be counted in the prior session's profile).
recomputeBinsFromRaw(int startOffset, int endOffset) =>
    array.fill(vpBins,     0.0)
    array.fill(vpBinsBull, 0.0)
    // v3.5: clamp to max_bars_back. A session can exceed 5000 bars on
    // a Daily anchor with <=15s charts, or a Weekly/Monthly anchor on
    // any intraday timeframe — `high[offset]` past max_bars_back (5000)
    // throws a runtime error and crashes the indicator. Clamping caps
    // the profile at the most-recent 5000 bars of the session: degraded
    // coverage on those extreme configs, but no crash.
    int safeEnd = math.min(endOffset, 4999)
    if safeEnd >= startOffset and not na(vpSessHigh) and not na(vpSessLow) and vpSessHigh > vpSessLow
        float binSize  = (vpSessHigh - vpSessLow) / vpRows
        bool  moneyFlow = vpSource == 'Money Flow'
        if binSize > 0
            for offset = startOffset to safeEnd
                float bH = high[offset]
                float bL = low[offset]
                float bC = close[offset]
                float bO = open[offset]
                float bV = nz(volume[offset])
                float bRange = bH - bL
                if bRange > 0 and bV > 0
                    // v3.5: 3-state bull fraction. A neutral bar — a doji
                    // (close==open) under Bar Polarity, or a close exactly
                    // at mid-range under Buying Pressure — contributes HALF
                    // its weight to bull, so it splits 50/50 bull/bear
                    // instead of being silently dumped entirely into bear.
                    // Matches the v2.1 doji-neutral treatment for icebergs.
                    float bullFrac = vpSentimentMethod == 'Bar Polarity' ? (bC > bO ? 1.0 : bC < bO ? 0.0 : 0.5) : ((bC - bL) > (bH - bC) ? 1.0 : (bC - bL) < (bH - bC) ? 0.0 : 0.5)
                    for i = 0 to vpRows - 1
                        float binLow  = vpSessLow + i * binSize
                        float binHigh = binLow + binSize
                        float overlap = math.max(0.0, math.min(bH, binHigh) - math.max(bL, binLow))
                        if overlap > 0
                            float ratio       = overlap / bRange
                            float binMidPrice = binLow + binSize * 0.5
                            float weight      = moneyFlow ? bV * ratio * binMidPrice : bV * ratio
                            array.set(vpBins,     i, array.get(vpBins,     i) + weight)
                            array.set(vpBinsBull, i, array.get(vpBinsBull, i) + weight * bullFrac)
    0

// Incremental: add ONLY the current bar's volume into the existing bin array
// using the current session range. Safe to call when the range is unchanged
// from the last full recompute — bin boundaries are stable, so adding to
// existing indices is correct. O(vpRows) per call.
accumulateCurrentBar() =>
    if not na(vpSessHigh) and not na(vpSessLow) and vpSessHigh > vpSessLow
        float binSize  = (vpSessHigh - vpSessLow) / vpRows
        float barRange = high - low
        float vol      = nz(volume)
        if barRange > 0 and binSize > 0 and vol > 0
            // v3.5: 3-state bull fraction — see recomputeBinsFromRaw.
            float bullFrac = vpSentimentMethod == 'Bar Polarity' ? (close > open ? 1.0 : close < open ? 0.0 : 0.5) : ((close - low) > (high - close) ? 1.0 : (close - low) < (high - close) ? 0.0 : 0.5)
            bool moneyFlow = vpSource == 'Money Flow'
            for i = 0 to vpRows - 1
                float binLow  = vpSessLow + i * binSize
                float binHigh = binLow + binSize
                float overlap = math.max(0.0, math.min(high, binHigh) - math.max(low, binLow))
                if overlap > 0
                    float ratio       = overlap / barRange
                    float binMidPrice = binLow + binSize * 0.5
                    float weight      = moneyFlow ? vol * ratio * binMidPrice : vol * ratio
                    array.set(vpBins,     i, array.get(vpBins,     i) + weight)
                    array.set(vpBinsBull, i, array.get(vpBinsBull, i) + weight * bullFrac)
    0

//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// HELPERS — Composite VP (v3.0)
//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Re-aggregate all stored session bins onto a unified composite price grid
// spanning [min(all session lows), max(all session highs)]. Each session's
// bins are redistributed onto the composite grid via overlap ratios — same
// math as recomputeBinsFromRaw, but the source is per-session-bin snapshots
// rather than raw bar history (each session was already recomputed
// drift-free at finalize time, so the snapshot IS the accurate distribution).
// Cost: O(N_sessions × vpRows) since v3.5 (each source bin maps directly
// to its ~1-3 overlapping composite bins instead of scanning all vpRows).
// Called only on session finalize, so per-bar amortised cost is negligible.
//
// Pine v6 forbids modifying global scalar `var`s from inside user-defined
// functions, so this returns a 5-tuple [rangeHigh, rangeLow, POC, VAH, VAL]
// and the caller assigns to the globals. The composite BIN array IS mutated
// in-place — that's allowed because array contents are reference-mutable
// (only scalar reassignment is forbidden).
recomputeComposite() =>
    float retHigh = na
    float retLow  = na
    float retPOC  = na
    float retVAH  = na
    float retVAL  = na
    int nSess = matrix.rows(compositeSessionBins)
    if nSess > 0
        float cHigh = -1.0e30
        float cLow  =  1.0e30
        for i = 0 to nSess - 1
            cHigh := math.max(cHigh, array.get(compositeSessionHighs, i))
            cLow  := math.min(cLow,  array.get(compositeSessionLows,  i))
        retHigh := cHigh
        retLow  := cLow
        array.fill(compositeBins, 0.0)
        if cHigh > cLow
            float compBinSize = (cHigh - cLow) / vpRows
            for s = 0 to nSess - 1
                float sHigh = array.get(compositeSessionHighs, s)
                float sLow  = array.get(compositeSessionLows,  s)
                if sHigh > sLow
                    float sBinSize = (sHigh - sLow) / vpRows
                    for j = 0 to vpRows - 1
                        float bV = matrix.get(compositeSessionBins, s, j)
                        if bV > 0
                            float bLowP  = sLow + j * sBinSize
                            float bHighP = bLowP + sBinSize
                            // v3.5: a source bin overlaps only a contiguous
                            // run of composite bins — compute that index
                            // range directly instead of scanning all vpRows.
                            // Drops the merge from O(N·R²) to O(N·R) (each
                            // source bin now touches ~1-3 composite bins, +2
                            // padding). Pad ±1 and clamp for floating-point
                            // safety; the `overlap > 0` test filters slack.
                            int kStart = math.max(0,         int(math.floor((bLowP  - cLow) / compBinSize)) - 1)
                            int kEnd   = math.min(vpRows - 1, int(math.floor((bHighP - cLow) / compBinSize)) + 1)
                            for k = kStart to kEnd
                                float cLowP  = cLow + k * compBinSize
                                float cHighP = cLowP + compBinSize
                                float overlap = math.max(0.0, math.min(bHighP, cHighP) - math.max(bLowP, cLowP))
                                if overlap > 0
                                    float ratio = overlap / sBinSize
                                    array.set(compositeBins, k, array.get(compositeBins, k) + bV * ratio)
            [cPocIdx, cVaL, cVaH, cTotalV] = computeProfile(compositeBins, vpRows, vpValueAreaP)
            if cTotalV > 0
                retPOC := cLow + (cPocIdx + 0.5) * compBinSize
                retVAH := cLow + (cVaH + 1) * compBinSize
                retVAL := cLow + cVaL * compBinSize
    [retHigh, retLow, retPOC, retVAH, retVAL]

//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// HELPERS — confluence
//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Returns a confluence description string, empty if none. Checks the pivot
// price against previous-session levels, active naked POCs, and the AVWAP/σ
// bands at the pivot bar (offset back by `barOffset`).
checkConfluence(float price, float tickDist, int barOffset) =>
    string out = ''
    if not confEnabled or na(price)
        out
    else
        float td = tickDist * syminfo.mintick
        // Current developing levels at the PIVOT BAR (barOffset bars back).
        // v2.7: must use [barOffset] indexing. The SMT block evaluates at
        // the top of each bar — BEFORE VP section 4 publishes the new
        // `currDevPOC/VAH/VAL`. So at confirmation bar B reading
        // `currDevPOC` (no index) returns end-of-bar-(B-1)'s value, but
        // the pivot itself is at bar B-pivotRightLen (callers pass
        // pivotRightLen as barOffset since v3.3). The drift between those
        // two POC samples silently masked legitimate currDev confluence
        // on historical pivots.
        // v2.6 published these values correctly; the bug was that SMT was
        // reading the wrong bar's snapshot. `currDevPOC[barOffset]` gives
        // the developing POC as of the pivot bar — which is what
        // "★ confluence at this pivot" actually means.
        float pivDevPOC = currDevPOC[barOffset]
        float pivDevVAH = currDevVAH[barOffset]
        float pivDevVAL = currDevVAL[barOffset]
        if not na(pivDevPOC) and math.abs(price - pivDevPOC) <= td
            out := out + 'POC '
        if not na(pivDevVAH) and math.abs(price - pivDevVAH) <= td
            out := out + 'VAH '
        if not na(pivDevVAL) and math.abs(price - pivDevVAL) <= td
            out := out + 'VAL '
        // Previous session levels — v3.4: now [barOffset] indexed, matching
        // currDev and composite. A pivot in the last `pivotRightLen` bars
        // of a session is confirmed AFTER the session boundary, by which
        // point `prevSessPOC` (no index) has already advanced to the
        // just-finalized session. Indexing reads the prev-session levels
        // as they stood AT the pivot bar — so a near-boundary pivot is
        // evaluated against the session that was genuinely "previous" at
        // its time, not the one finalized a few bars later.
        float  pivPrevPOC  = prevSessPOC[barOffset]
        float  pivPrevVAH  = prevSessVAH[barOffset]
        float  pivPrevVAL  = prevSessVAL[barOffset]
        string pivPrevSent = prevSessPOCSentiment[barOffset]
        bool atPVAH = not na(pivPrevVAH) and math.abs(price - pivPrevVAH) <= td
        bool atPVAL = not na(pivPrevVAL) and math.abs(price - pivPrevVAL) <= td
        if not na(pivPrevPOC) and math.abs(price - pivPrevPOC) <= td
            string sentSuffix = na(pivPrevSent) or pivPrevSent == 'Neutral' ? '' : '(' + pivPrevSent + ')'
            out := out + 'pPOC' + sentSuffix + ' '
        if atPVAH
            out := out + 'pVAH '
        if atPVAL
            out := out + 'pVAL '
        // InVA fires only when CLEARLY inside the value area (strictly past
        // both edges by more than the tick tolerance). Prevents redundant
        // "pVAH InVA" tag pairs on boundary-hugging prices.
        if not atPVAH and not atPVAL and not na(pivPrevVAH) and not na(pivPrevVAL) and price > pivPrevVAL + td and price < pivPrevVAH - td
            out := out + 'InVA '
        // Composite (multi-session aggregate) levels — added in v3.0.
        // [barOffset] indexed for the same reason as currDev — the SMT
        // block reads these at the top of the bar before any v3.0
        // session-finalize update. In practice composite only updates on
        // session boundaries, so the indexed and non-indexed reads return
        // the same value EXCEPT for pivots that fired in a prior session
        // (where indexing correctly returns that earlier session's
        // composite snapshot).
        // v3.1: gate on `compositeSessionCount[barOffset] >= 2`. With a
        // single session in the composite, cPOC == pPOC by construction
        // — firing both tags double-counts the same level and inflates
        // the ★N strength count. Requiring >= 2 sessions ensures the
        // composite is meaningfully different from the immediate-prev
        // session reference.
        float pivComPOC   = compositePOC[barOffset]
        float pivComVAH   = compositeVAH[barOffset]
        float pivComVAL   = compositeVAL[barOffset]
        int   pivCompSess = compositeSessionCount[barOffset]
        if not na(pivComPOC) and pivCompSess >= 2 and math.abs(price - pivComPOC) <= td
            out := out + 'cPOC '
        if not na(pivComVAH) and pivCompSess >= 2 and math.abs(price - pivComVAH) <= td
            out := out + 'cVAH '
        if not na(pivComVAL) and pivCompSess >= 2 and math.abs(price - pivComVAL) <= td
            out := out + 'cVAL '
        // Naked POCs — v3.0: removed `break` so a pivot near multiple
        // nPOCs (e.g., 1.33995 and 1.34005 with confTicks=10) tags BOTH
        // instead of silently dropping the second match.
        int sz = array.size(nakedPOCs)
        if sz > 0
            for i = 0 to sz - 1
                float p = array.get(nakedPOCs, i)
                if math.abs(price - p) <= td
                    out := out + 'nPOC@' + str.tostring(p, format.mintick) + ' '
        // AVWAP + σ bands at the pivot bar. Require pivSigma > 0 to avoid
        // false-positive confluence on session-boundary bars, where the
        // AVWAP has only 1 bar of accumulation and equals hlc3 of that bar
        // (so any nearby price would otherwise "match").
        if avwapEnabled
            float pivAvwap = avwap[barOffset]
            float pivSigma = avwapSigma[barOffset]
            if not na(pivAvwap) and not na(pivSigma) and pivSigma > 0 and math.abs(price - pivAvwap) <= td
                out := out + 'AVWAP '
            if not na(pivAvwap) and not na(pivSigma) and pivSigma > 0
                if showSigma1 and math.abs(price - (pivAvwap + sigma1Mult * pivSigma)) <= td
                    out := out + '+' + str.tostring(sigma1Mult, '#.#') + 'σ '
                if showSigma1 and math.abs(price - (pivAvwap - sigma1Mult * pivSigma)) <= td
                    out := out + '-' + str.tostring(sigma1Mult, '#.#') + 'σ '
                if showSigma2 and math.abs(price - (pivAvwap + sigma2Mult * pivSigma)) <= td
                    out := out + '+' + str.tostring(sigma2Mult, '#.#') + 'σ '
                if showSigma2 and math.abs(price - (pivAvwap - sigma2Mult * pivSigma)) <= td
                    out := out + '-' + str.tostring(sigma2Mult, '#.#') + 'σ '
                if showSigma3 and math.abs(price - (pivAvwap + sigma3Mult * pivSigma)) <= td
                    out := out + '+' + str.tostring(sigma3Mult, '#.#') + 'σ '
                if showSigma3 and math.abs(price - (pivAvwap - sigma3Mult * pivSigma)) <= td
                    out := out + '-' + str.tostring(sigma3Mult, '#.#') + 'σ '
        // Strip the trailing space left by the tag appends.
        if str.endswith(out, ' ')
            out := str.substring(out, 0, str.length(out) - 1)
        out

// Returns a string listing which tracked levels lie inside [barLow, barHigh].
// Used for iceberg confluence — we care whether the bar's whole range
// straddled a level, not just whether close was near it.
levelsInBar(float barLow, float barHigh, int barOffset) =>
    string out = ''
    if barHigh >= barLow
        // Developing-session levels at the bar being checked. v2.7: explicit
        // [barOffset] indexing for symmetry with checkConfluence. Iceberg
        // calls with barOffset=0 so currDevPOC[0]==currDevPOC (no behaviour
        // change); the indexed form is robust to any future nonzero caller.
        float barDevPOC = currDevPOC[barOffset]
        float barDevVAH = currDevVAH[barOffset]
        float barDevVAL = currDevVAL[barOffset]
        if not na(barDevPOC) and barDevPOC >= barLow and barDevPOC <= barHigh
            out := out + 'POC '
        if not na(barDevVAH) and barDevVAH >= barLow and barDevVAH <= barHigh
            out := out + 'VAH '
        if not na(barDevVAL) and barDevVAL >= barLow and barDevVAL <= barHigh
            out := out + 'VAL '
        // Previous-session levels — v3.4: [barOffset] indexed for symmetry
        // with checkConfluence. Iceberg calls with barOffset=0 so this is
        // currently equivalent to the un-indexed read (no behaviour change),
        // but the indexed form is correct for any future nonzero caller.
        float  barPrevPOC  = prevSessPOC[barOffset]
        float  barPrevVAH  = prevSessVAH[barOffset]
        float  barPrevVAL  = prevSessVAL[barOffset]
        string barPrevSent = prevSessPOCSentiment[barOffset]
        if not na(barPrevPOC) and barPrevPOC >= barLow and barPrevPOC <= barHigh
            string sentSuffix = na(barPrevSent) or barPrevSent == 'Neutral' ? '' : '(' + barPrevSent + ')'
            out := out + 'pPOC' + sentSuffix + ' '
        if not na(barPrevVAH) and barPrevVAH >= barLow and barPrevVAH <= barHigh
            out := out + 'pVAH '
        if not na(barPrevVAL) and barPrevVAL >= barLow and barPrevVAL <= barHigh
            out := out + 'pVAL '
        // Composite (multi-session aggregate) levels — added in v3.0.
        // v3.1: same min-2-sessions gate as checkConfluence (see comment
        // there) — composite IS prev-session when N=1, so cPOC+pPOC
        // would double-fire.
        float barComPOC   = compositePOC[barOffset]
        float barComVAH   = compositeVAH[barOffset]
        float barComVAL   = compositeVAL[barOffset]
        int   barCompSess = compositeSessionCount[barOffset]
        if not na(barComPOC) and barCompSess >= 2 and barComPOC >= barLow and barComPOC <= barHigh
            out := out + 'cPOC '
        if not na(barComVAH) and barCompSess >= 2 and barComVAH >= barLow and barComVAH <= barHigh
            out := out + 'cVAH '
        if not na(barComVAL) and barCompSess >= 2 and barComVAL >= barLow and barComVAL <= barHigh
            out := out + 'cVAL '
        // Naked POCs — v3.0: removed `break` so a bar straddling multiple
        // nPOCs tags all of them, not just the first.
        int sz = array.size(nakedPOCs)
        if sz > 0
            for i = 0 to sz - 1
                float p = array.get(nakedPOCs, i)
                if p >= barLow and p <= barHigh
                    out := out + 'nPOC@' + str.tostring(p, format.mintick) + ' '
        if avwapEnabled
            float pivAvwap = avwap[barOffset]
            float pivSigma = avwapSigma[barOffset]
            // Require pivSigma > 0 (same reasoning as checkConfluence — skips
            // session-boundary bars where AVWAP has only 1 bar of accumulation).
            if not na(pivAvwap) and not na(pivSigma) and pivSigma > 0 and pivAvwap >= barLow and pivAvwap <= barHigh
                out := out + 'AVWAP '
            if not na(pivAvwap) and not na(pivSigma) and pivSigma > 0
                float u1 = pivAvwap + sigma1Mult * pivSigma
                float l1 = pivAvwap - sigma1Mult * pivSigma
                float u2 = pivAvwap + sigma2Mult * pivSigma
                float l2 = pivAvwap - sigma2Mult * pivSigma
                float u3 = pivAvwap + sigma3Mult * pivSigma
                float l3 = pivAvwap - sigma3Mult * pivSigma
                if showSigma1 and u1 >= barLow and u1 <= barHigh
                    out := out + '+' + str.tostring(sigma1Mult, '#.#') + 'σ '
                if showSigma1 and l1 >= barLow and l1 <= barHigh
                    out := out + '-' + str.tostring(sigma1Mult, '#.#') + 'σ '
                if showSigma2 and u2 >= barLow and u2 <= barHigh
                    out := out + '+' + str.tostring(sigma2Mult, '#.#') + 'σ '
                if showSigma2 and l2 >= barLow and l2 <= barHigh
                    out := out + '-' + str.tostring(sigma2Mult, '#.#') + 'σ '
                if showSigma3 and u3 >= barLow and u3 <= barHigh
                    out := out + '+' + str.tostring(sigma3Mult, '#.#') + 'σ '
                if showSigma3 and l3 >= barLow and l3 <= barHigh
                    out := out + '-' + str.tostring(sigma3Mult, '#.#') + 'σ '
    // Strip the trailing space left by the tag appends.
    if str.endswith(out, ' ')
        out := str.substring(out, 0, str.length(out) - 1)
    out

//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// SMT DIVERGENCE
//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Combined divergence drawing — ONE line + ONE label per pivot, listing
// all diverging symbols. Prevents visual stacking when multiple comparison
// symbols diverge against the same chart pivot (each was drawing its own
// line/label at identical coordinates, so only the last one was visible).
// The confluence flag adds a ★N marker (where N = number of tags) to the
// visible label and a confluence-levels breakdown to the tooltip.

// v3.0: count of space-separated confluence tags in the string. Used to
// surface confluence STRENGTH at a glance — "POC pPOC(Bull) AVWAP +1.0σ"
// returns 4 → label shows ★4 instead of just ★. Distinguishes strong
// (multi-tag) pivots from single-tag ones in the label, tooltip,
// dashboard, and alert message.
countConfluenceTags(string s) =>
    str.length(s) == 0 ? 0 : array.size(str.split(s, ' '))

drawDivergence(bool isBull, int prevBar, float prevChart, float currChart, string symList, bool hasConf, string confluenceStr, color col) =>
    int curBar = bar_index - pivotRightLen   // v3.3: pivot is pivotRightLen bars back at confirmation
    // v3.6: safeLeftBar clamp on the previous-pivot endpoint — guards
    // RE10026 if two consecutive SMT pivots are an extreme distance apart
    // (rare on intraday, but possible). Clamping only shifts the line's
    // left end; the label still carries the full divergence detail.
    line.new(safeLeftBar(prevBar), prevChart, curBar, currChart, color = col, width = lineWidth, style = lineStyle)
    if showLabel
        float midPrice = (prevChart + currChart) / 2.0
        int   midBar   = math.round((prevBar + curBar) / 2.0)
        int    confCount = hasConf ? countConfluenceTags(confluenceStr) : 0
        string starMark  = hasConf ? ' ★' + str.tostring(confCount) : ''
        string tip = 'Chart: ' + str.tostring(prevChart, format.mintick) + ' → ' + str.tostring(currChart, format.mintick) + '\nDiverging vs: ' + symList + (hasConf ? '\n★ Confluence (' + str.tostring(confCount) + '): ' + confluenceStr : '')
        label.new(midBar, midPrice, (isBull ? 'Bull SMT' : 'Bear SMT') + starMark + '\n' + symList, style = isBull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = col, textcolor = color.white, size = lblSize, tooltip = tip)

// Pre-compute confluence strings for the pivot prices at top-level scope.
// Pine v6 warns about calling user-defined functions inside conditional
// blocks if they reference historical series (avwap[], avwapSigma[]) —
// the function may develop gaps in its internal series history. Calling
// them every bar with phVal / plVal (which are `na` on non-pivot bars)
// is harmless because the function early-returns an empty string on na.
string smtBearConf = checkConfluence(phVal, confTicks, pivotRightLen)
string smtBullConf = checkConfluence(plVal, confTicks, pivotRightLen)

// ─── Bearish SMT (confirmed pivot HIGH) ─────────────────────────────────────
// Per-pivot dedup: collect every symbol that diverges, then update dashboard
// state ONCE and fire ONE combined alert. Avoids three alerts + the dashboard
// only showing whichever symbol happened to be evaluated last.
//
// Inverse-correlation sampling: at a chart pivot HIGH the chart price is
// peaking, so a TRUE inverse cmp should be at a pivot LOW. We sample the
// cmp's LOW (not HIGH) at the chart's pivot-high bar so we compare the
// "matching" cmp pivot value across consecutive chart pivots.
if not na(phVal)
    int pivotBar = bar_index - pivotRightLen
    float s1At = sym1Corr == 'Inverse' ? s1Low[pivotRightLen]  : s1High[pivotRightLen]
    float s2At = sym2Corr == 'Inverse' ? s2Low[pivotRightLen]  : s2High[pivotRightLen]
    float s3At = sym3Corr == 'Inverse' ? s3Low[pivotRightLen]  : s3High[pivotRightLen]

    if not na(prevPHChart)
        bool chartHH = phVal > prevPHChart
        bool chartLH = phVal < prevPHChart
        string conf = smtBearConf   // pre-computed at top-level for Pine consistency

        int    divCount     = 0
        string divergedSyms = ''

        if sym1Enabled and not na(s1At) and not na(prevPHS1)
            bool s1HH = s1At > prevPHS1
            bool s1LH = s1At < prevPHS1
            // Positive: divergence when directions OPPOSE.  Inverse: divergence when directions MATCH.
            bool d1 = sym1Corr == 'Positive' ? ((chartHH and s1LH) or (chartLH and s1HH)) : ((chartHH and s1HH) or (chartLH and s1LH))
            if d1
                divergedSyms := divergedSyms + (divCount > 0 ? ', ' : '') + shortName(sym1) + (sym1Corr == 'Inverse' ? ' (inv)' : '')
                divCount     += 1

        if sym2Enabled and not na(s2At) and not na(prevPHS2)
            bool s2HH = s2At > prevPHS2
            bool s2LH = s2At < prevPHS2
            bool d2 = sym2Corr == 'Positive' ? ((chartHH and s2LH) or (chartLH and s2HH)) : ((chartHH and s2HH) or (chartLH and s2LH))
            if d2
                divergedSyms := divergedSyms + (divCount > 0 ? ', ' : '') + shortName(sym2) + (sym2Corr == 'Inverse' ? ' (inv)' : '')
                divCount     += 1

        if sym3Enabled and not na(s3At) and not na(prevPHS3)
            bool s3HH = s3At > prevPHS3
            bool s3LH = s3At < prevPHS3
            bool d3 = sym3Corr == 'Positive' ? ((chartHH and s3LH) or (chartLH and s3HH)) : ((chartHH and s3HH) or (chartLH and s3LH))
            if d3
                divergedSyms := divergedSyms + (divCount > 0 ? ', ' : '') + shortName(sym3) + (sym3Corr == 'Inverse' ? ' (inv)' : '')
                divCount     += 1

        if divCount > 0
            bool   hasConf = str.length(conf) > 0
            // ONE combined line + label for the pivot (was previously drawn
            // once per diverging symbol, causing visual overlap).
            drawDivergence(false, prevPHBar, prevPHChart, phVal, divergedSyms, hasConf, conf, bearColor)
            lastBearBar       := pivotBar
            lastBearSym       := divergedSyms
            lastBearPrice     := phVal
            lastBearConf      := hasConf
            lastBearConfCount := hasConf ? countConfluenceTags(conf) : 0
            if alertBear
                string base = 'Bearish SMT vs ' + divergedSyms
                string msg  = hasConf ? base + ' | ★' + str.tostring(lastBearConfCount) + ' Confluence: ' + conf : base
                alert(msg, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

    prevPHChart := phVal
    prevPHS1    := s1At
    prevPHS2    := s2At
    prevPHS3    := s3At
    prevPHBar   := pivotBar

// ─── Bullish SMT (confirmed pivot LOW) ──────────────────────────────────────
// NOTE: structurally symmetric with the bearish block above. Any logic
//       changes (dedup, confluence handling, drawing, alert formatting)
//       MUST be applied to both blocks identically.
//
// Inverse sampling (mirror of the bearish block): at a chart pivot LOW the
// chart price is troughing, so a TRUE inverse cmp should be at a pivot HIGH.
// We sample cmp's HIGH (not LOW) at the chart's pivot-low bar.
if not na(plVal)
    int pivotBar = bar_index - pivotRightLen
    float s1At = sym1Corr == 'Inverse' ? s1High[pivotRightLen] : s1Low[pivotRightLen]
    float s2At = sym2Corr == 'Inverse' ? s2High[pivotRightLen] : s2Low[pivotRightLen]
    float s3At = sym3Corr == 'Inverse' ? s3High[pivotRightLen] : s3Low[pivotRightLen]

    if not na(prevPLChart)
        bool chartLL = plVal < prevPLChart
        bool chartHL = plVal > prevPLChart
        string conf = smtBullConf   // pre-computed at top-level for Pine consistency

        int    divCount     = 0
        string divergedSyms = ''

        if sym1Enabled and not na(s1At) and not na(prevPLS1)
            bool s1LL = s1At < prevPLS1
            bool s1HL = s1At > prevPLS1
            // Positive: divergence when directions OPPOSE.  Inverse: divergence when directions MATCH.
            bool d1 = sym1Corr == 'Positive' ? ((chartLL and s1HL) or (chartHL and s1LL)) : ((chartLL and s1LL) or (chartHL and s1HL))
            if d1
                divergedSyms := divergedSyms + (divCount > 0 ? ', ' : '') + shortName(sym1) + (sym1Corr == 'Inverse' ? ' (inv)' : '')
                divCount     += 1

        if sym2Enabled and not na(s2At) and not na(prevPLS2)
            bool s2LL = s2At < prevPLS2
            bool s2HL = s2At > prevPLS2
            bool d2 = sym2Corr == 'Positive' ? ((chartLL and s2HL) or (chartHL and s2LL)) : ((chartLL and s2LL) or (chartHL and s2HL))
            if d2
                divergedSyms := divergedSyms + (divCount > 0 ? ', ' : '') + shortName(sym2) + (sym2Corr == 'Inverse' ? ' (inv)' : '')
                divCount     += 1

        if sym3Enabled and not na(s3At) and not na(prevPLS3)
            bool s3LL = s3At < prevPLS3
            bool s3HL = s3At > prevPLS3
            bool d3 = sym3Corr == 'Positive' ? ((chartLL and s3HL) or (chartHL and s3LL)) : ((chartLL and s3LL) or (chartHL and s3HL))
            if d3
                divergedSyms := divergedSyms + (divCount > 0 ? ', ' : '') + shortName(sym3) + (sym3Corr == 'Inverse' ? ' (inv)' : '')
                divCount     += 1

        if divCount > 0
            bool   hasConf = str.length(conf) > 0
            // ONE combined line + label for the pivot.
            drawDivergence(true, prevPLBar, prevPLChart, plVal, divergedSyms, hasConf, conf, bullColor)
            lastBullBar       := pivotBar
            lastBullSym       := divergedSyms
            lastBullPrice     := plVal
            lastBullConf      := hasConf
            lastBullConfCount := hasConf ? countConfluenceTags(conf) : 0
            if alertBull
                string base = 'Bullish SMT vs ' + divergedSyms
                string msg  = hasConf ? base + ' | ★' + str.tostring(lastBullConfCount) + ' Confluence: ' + conf : base
                alert(msg, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

    prevPLChart := plVal
    prevPLS1    := s1At
    prevPLS2    := s2At
    prevPLS3    := s3At
    prevPLBar   := pivotBar

plotshape(showPivotMarkers and not na(phVal), title = 'Pivot High', style = shape.triangledown, location = location.abovebar, color = color.new(GRAY, 0), size = size.tiny, offset = -pivotRightLen)
plotshape(showPivotMarkers and not na(plVal), title = 'Pivot Low',  style = shape.triangleup,   location = location.belowbar, color = color.new(GRAY, 0), size = size.tiny, offset = -pivotRightLen)

//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// VOLUME PROFILE — uses session boundary detection from the helpers section.
//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1) Session finalization — compute the just-completed session's POC/VAH/VAL
//    BEFORE we reset for the new session. Save as previous-session levels and
//    push the POC to the naked-POC list.
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if vpEnabled and isNewVPSession and not na(vpSessHigh) and vpSessHigh > vpSessLow
    // Recompute bins from the JUST-COMPLETED session's bars before computing
    // prev-session POC/VAH/VAL. offset 1 = previous bar (last bar of prior
    // session); offset bar_index - vpSessStart = first bar of prior session.
    // The current bar (offset 0) is the first bar of the NEW session and
    // must be excluded from prior-session aggregation.
    recomputeBinsFromRaw(1, bar_index - vpSessStart)
    [fPocIdx, fVaL, fVaH, fTotalV] = computeProfile(vpBins, vpRows, vpValueAreaP)
    if fTotalV > 0
        float fBinSize = (vpSessHigh - vpSessLow) / vpRows
        float fPOC = vpSessLow + (fPocIdx + 0.5) * fBinSize
        float fVAH = vpSessLow + (fVaH + 1) * fBinSize
        float fVAL = vpSessLow + fVaL * fBinSize

        // Save scalar levels.
        prevSessPOC := fPOC
        prevSessVAH := fVAH
        prevSessVAL := fVAL
        prevSessStartBar := vpSessStart
        prevSessEndBar   := bar_index - 1

        // POC bin sentiment — used to enrich confluence tags (pPOC(Bull/Bear)).
        // 60%+ bull = Bull, 40%- bull = Bear, otherwise Neutral.
        float fPocTotal = array.get(vpBins,     fPocIdx)
        float fPocBull  = array.get(vpBinsBull, fPocIdx)
        if fPocTotal > 0
            float bullRatio = fPocBull / fPocTotal
            prevSessPOCSentiment := bullRatio >= 0.6 ? 'Bull' : bullRatio <= 0.4 ? 'Bear' : 'Neutral'
        else
            prevSessPOCSentiment := 'Neutral'

        // Replace previous-session drawings.
        if not na(prevPocLine)
            line.delete(prevPocLine)
        if not na(prevVahLine)
            line.delete(prevVahLine)
        if not na(prevValLine)
            line.delete(prevValLine)
        if not na(prevPocLabel)
            label.delete(prevPocLabel)
        if not na(prevVahLabel)
            label.delete(prevVahLabel)
        if not na(prevValLabel)
            label.delete(prevValLabel)

        if vpShowPrev
            // v3.6: safeLeftBar clamp — prevSessStartBar can be 0 (first
            // session) which on a 1-min chart is >max_bars_back away → RE10026.
            int prevLineLeft = safeLeftBar(prevSessStartBar)
            prevPocLine := line.new(prevLineLeft, fPOC, prevSessEndBar, fPOC, color = vpPrevPocColor, width = vpPrevLineWidth, style = line.style_solid, extend = extend.right)
            prevVahLine := line.new(prevLineLeft, fVAH, prevSessEndBar, fVAH, color = vpPrevVaColor,  width = 1, style = line.style_dotted, extend = extend.right)
            prevValLine := line.new(prevLineLeft, fVAL, prevSessEndBar, fVAL, color = vpPrevVaColor,  width = 1, style = line.style_dotted, extend = extend.right)
            if vpShowLabels
                int prevLabelBar = bar_index + 1
                prevPocLabel := label.new(prevLabelBar, fPOC, 'pPOC ' + str.tostring(fPOC, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = vpPrevPocColor, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
                prevVahLabel := label.new(prevLabelBar, fVAH, 'pVAH ' + str.tostring(fVAH, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = vpPrevVaColor,  textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
                prevValLabel := label.new(prevLabelBar, fVAL, 'pVAL ' + str.tostring(fVAL, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = vpPrevVaColor,  textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)

        // Push the finalized POC onto the naked-POC list. NOTE: we store
        // `bar_index` (the current bar = creation bar) — not `prevSessStartBar`
        // — so the 1-bar grace period in the touch check actually works.
        // Using `prevSessStartBar` here is the previously-shipped bug: the
        // grace check `bar_index > created + 1` would have been true on the
        // very first bar of the new session (since prevSessStartBar is way
        // back), letting an opening-bar straddle invalidate the nPOC instantly.
        if nPocEnabled
            line nLine = line.new(safeLeftBar(prevSessStartBar), fPOC, bar_index, fPOC, color = nPocColor, width = 1, style = nPocStyle, extend = extend.right)
            label nLabel = nPocLabels ? label.new(bar_index + 1, fPOC, 'nPOC ' + str.tostring(fPOC, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = nPocColor, textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny) : na
            array.push(nakedPOCs,            fPOC)
            array.push(nakedPOCCreationBars, bar_index)
            array.push(nakedPOCLines,        nLine)
            array.push(nakedPOCLabels,       nLabel)

            // Prune oldest if over the max-tracked limit.
            while array.size(nakedPOCs) > nPocMax
                array.shift(nakedPOCs)
                array.shift(nakedPOCCreationBars)
                line   oldL  = array.shift(nakedPOCLines)
                label  oldLb = array.shift(nakedPOCLabels)
                line.delete(oldL)
                if not na(oldLb)
                    label.delete(oldLb)

        // Composite VP — snapshot the just-finalized session's bins into
        // the rolling N-session matrix, then re-aggregate. vpBins still
        // holds the prior session's final volume distribution (the
        // recomputeBinsFromRaw at the top of this block produced it; the
        // section-3 reset that clears vpBins hasn't run yet). v3.0 feature.
        if vpCompositeEnabled
            array<float> sessBinsCopy = array.copy(vpBins)
            matrix.add_row(compositeSessionBins, matrix.rows(compositeSessionBins), sessBinsCopy)
            array.push(compositeSessionHighs,     vpSessHigh)
            array.push(compositeSessionLows,      vpSessLow)
            array.push(compositeSessionStartBars, vpSessStart)
            // Trim oldest if over the rolling-window cap. Keep all four
            // arrays in lock-step.
            while matrix.rows(compositeSessionBins) > vpCompositeSessions
                matrix.remove_row(compositeSessionBins, 0)
                array.shift(compositeSessionHighs)
                array.shift(compositeSessionLows)
                array.shift(compositeSessionStartBars)
            // Pine v6 forbids the function from reassigning scalar globals,
            // so it returns a 5-tuple — we assign here at the call site.
            [cRH, cRL, cP, cVH, cVL] = recomputeComposite()
            compositeRangeHigh     := cRH
            compositeRangeLow      := cRL
            compositePOC           := cP
            compositeVAH           := cVH
            compositeVAL           := cVL
            compositeSessionCount  := matrix.rows(compositeSessionBins)
            // Replace composite drawings.
            if not na(compositePocLine)
                line.delete(compositePocLine)
            if not na(compositeVahLine)
                line.delete(compositeVahLine)
            if not na(compositeValLine)
                line.delete(compositeValLine)
            if not na(compositePocLabel)
                label.delete(compositePocLabel)
            if not na(compositeVahLabel)
                label.delete(compositeVahLabel)
            if not na(compositeValLabel)
                label.delete(compositeValLabel)
            // v3.1 fix: anchor the composite line at the OLDEST tracked
            // session's start, not at prevSessEndBar. Visually consistent
            // with prev-session lines (which span their session). The
            // line now visibly spans every session that contributed to
            // the composite, then extends right.
            int compLineLeft = safeLeftBar(array.size(compositeSessionStartBars) > 0 ? array.get(compositeSessionStartBars, 0) : prevSessStartBar)
            if not na(compositePOC)
                compositePocLine := line.new(compLineLeft, compositePOC, bar_index, compositePOC, color = vpCompositePocColor, width = vpCompositeWidth, style = line.style_solid, extend = extend.right)
            if not na(compositeVAH)
                compositeVahLine := line.new(compLineLeft, compositeVAH, bar_index, compositeVAH, color = vpCompositeVaColor, width = 1, style = line.style_dashed, extend = extend.right)
            if not na(compositeVAL)
                compositeValLine := line.new(compLineLeft, compositeVAL, bar_index, compositeVAL, color = vpCompositeVaColor, width = 1, style = line.style_dashed, extend = extend.right)
            if vpShowCompositeLabels
                int cLabelBar = bar_index + 4   // offset so labels don't overlap pPOC/nPOC labels at bar_index+1
                if not na(compositePOC)
                    compositePocLabel := label.new(cLabelBar, compositePOC, 'cPOC ' + str.tostring(compositePOC, format.mintick) + ' (' + str.tostring(compositeSessionCount) + ')', style = label.style_label_left, color = vpCompositePocColor, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
                if not na(compositeVAH)
                    compositeVahLabel := label.new(cLabelBar, compositeVAH, 'cVAH ' + str.tostring(compositeVAH, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = vpCompositeVaColor, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
                if not na(compositeVAL)
                    compositeValLabel := label.new(cLabelBar, compositeVAL, 'cVAL ' + str.tostring(compositeVAL, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = vpCompositeVaColor, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 2) Naked POC touch check — remove any whose price was touched this bar.
//    Skip the bar of creation (grace period) so a session-end straddle doesn't
//    instantly invalidate the just-created POC.
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if vpEnabled and nPocEnabled and barstate.isconfirmed and array.size(nakedPOCs) > 0
    int origSz = array.size(nakedPOCs)
    for n = 0 to origSz - 1
        int idx = origSz - 1 - n
        if idx < array.size(nakedPOCs)
            int created = array.get(nakedPOCCreationBars, idx)
            // 1-bar grace as documented — skip only the creation bar itself.
            // (Previously `> created + 1` was actually a 2-bar grace.)
            if bar_index > created
                float p = array.get(nakedPOCs, idx)
                if high >= p and low <= p
                    line  oldL  = array.get(nakedPOCLines, idx)
                    label oldLb = array.get(nakedPOCLabels, idx)
                    line.delete(oldL)
                    if not na(oldLb)
                        label.delete(oldLb)
                    array.remove(nakedPOCs,            idx)
                    array.remove(nakedPOCCreationBars, idx)
                    array.remove(nakedPOCLines,        idx)
                    array.remove(nakedPOCLabels,       idx)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 3) Session reset — clears developing-profile drawings refs (orphans them as
//    historical), resets aggregates.
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if vpEnabled and (isNewVPSession or na(vpSessHigh))
    // Histogram boxes (vol + sentiment) move to orphan arrays so they
    // remain visible as historical profile reference, anchored at the past
    // session's right edge. We track the box count from each session so we
    // can evict the OLDEST whole sessions when vpMaxOrphanSessions is
    // exceeded — gives predictable, user-controlled history depth instead
    // of letting Pine's 500-box budget silently FIFO-drop random drawings.
    int origVolBoxCount = array.size(vpBoxes)
    if origVolBoxCount > 0
        for j = 0 to origVolBoxCount - 1
            array.push(orphanedVpBoxes, array.get(vpBoxes, j))
        array.clear(vpBoxes)
        array.push(orphanedVolSizes, origVolBoxCount)
    int origSentBoxCount = array.size(vpSentBoxes)
    if origSentBoxCount > 0
        for j = 0 to origSentBoxCount - 1
            array.push(orphanedVpSentBoxes, array.get(vpSentBoxes, j))
        array.clear(vpSentBoxes)
        array.push(orphanedSentSizes, origSentBoxCount)

    // Evict oldest sessions if over the user's history cap. Each iteration
    // shifts off one session's tracked size + that many boxes.
    while array.size(orphanedVolSizes) > vpMaxOrphanSessions
        int oldestVolSize = array.shift(orphanedVolSizes)
        for j = 0 to oldestVolSize - 1
            box.delete(array.shift(orphanedVpBoxes))
    while array.size(orphanedSentSizes) > vpMaxOrphanSessions
        int oldestSentSize = array.shift(orphanedSentSizes)
        for j = 0 to oldestSentSize - 1
            box.delete(array.shift(orphanedVpSentBoxes))

    // HVN/LVN lines/zones, per-bin labels, heatmap overlays, and the dev
    // POC trail are session-specific markers that would clutter subsequent
    // sessions OR span across them visually. Explicitly DELETE these.
    if array.size(vpHVNLines) > 0
        for j = 0 to array.size(vpHVNLines) - 1
            line.delete(array.get(vpHVNLines, j))
        array.clear(vpHVNLines)
    if array.size(vpHVNZoneBoxes) > 0
        for j = 0 to array.size(vpHVNZoneBoxes) - 1
            box.delete(array.get(vpHVNZoneBoxes, j))
        array.clear(vpHVNZoneBoxes)
    if array.size(vpHeatmapBoxes) > 0
        for j = 0 to array.size(vpHeatmapBoxes) - 1
            box.delete(array.get(vpHeatmapBoxes, j))
        array.clear(vpHeatmapBoxes)
    if array.size(vpBinLabels) > 0
        for j = 0 to array.size(vpBinLabels) - 1
            label.delete(array.get(vpBinLabels, j))
        array.clear(vpBinLabels)
    array.clear(pocTrailPoints)
    if not na(pocTrailPolyline)
        polyline.delete(pocTrailPolyline)
        pocTrailPolyline := na
    // v3.4 fix: DELETE the developing POC/VAH/VAL lines + labels before
    // nulling the refs. Previously they were only set to `na`, orphaning
    // the line objects on the chart. With extend.right the orphaned
    // developing-POC line stayed visible and overlapped the prevPocLine
    // that section 1 draws for the SAME session's finalized POC — visual
    // duplication, and one stale line/label set leaked per session,
    // slowly eating the 500 line/label budget. HVN lines, heatmap boxes,
    // and bin labels just above were already deleted properly; the
    // POC/VAH/VAL lines were the inconsistency.
    if not na(vpPocLine)
        line.delete(vpPocLine)
    if not na(vpVahLine)
        line.delete(vpVahLine)
    if not na(vpValLine)
        line.delete(vpValLine)
    if not na(vpPocLabel)
        label.delete(vpPocLabel)
    if not na(vpVahLabel)
        label.delete(vpVahLabel)
    if not na(vpValLabel)
        label.delete(vpValLabel)
    if not na(vpHighLabel)
        label.delete(vpHighLabel)
    if not na(vpLowLabel)
        label.delete(vpLowLabel)
    vpPocLine   := na
    vpVahLine   := na
    vpValLine   := na
    vpPocLabel  := na
    vpVahLabel  := na
    vpValLabel  := na
    vpHighLabel := na
    vpLowLabel  := na
    // Reset session aggregates.
    vpSessHigh  := high
    vpSessLow   := low
    vpSessStart := bar_index
    array.fill(vpBins,     0.0)
    array.fill(vpBinsBull, 0.0)
    currDevPOC := na
    currDevVAH := na
    currDevVAL := na
    hvnCount := 0
    lvnCount := 0
    vpSessBarCount := 1
    lastRecompHigh := na
    lastRecompLow  := na
else if vpEnabled
    vpSessHigh := math.max(vpSessHigh, high)
    vpSessLow  := math.min(vpSessLow, low)
    if barstate.isconfirmed
        vpSessBarCount := vpSessBarCount + 1

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 4) Bin recomputation — drift-free, incremental when stable.
//    The previous v2.0 implementation did a full `recomputeBinsFromRaw` on
//    every confirmed bar — correct but O(N²·R) cumulatively across a session.
//    On extreme combos (Weekly+ anchor on M1 + vpRows=80) the late-session
//    recomputes exceeded Pine's per-bar loop budget.
//    The fix: only do a full recompute when the session range has actually
//    changed since the last recompute. While the range is stable, just add
//    the current bar's volume incrementally — bins are already aligned
//    correctly. Typical session: 5-10 recomputes (early), N-K incrementals.
//    Worst case (range expands every bar) degrades back to O(N²·R), same as
//    before — but typical case becomes O(N·R), matching naive incremental
//    approach in cost while remaining drift-free.
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if vpEnabled and barstate.isconfirmed and not na(vpSessHigh) and vpSessHigh > vpSessLow
    bool rangeChanged = na(lastRecompHigh) or na(lastRecompLow) or vpSessHigh != lastRecompHigh or vpSessLow != lastRecompLow
    if rangeChanged
        recomputeBinsFromRaw(0, bar_index - vpSessStart)
        lastRecompHigh := vpSessHigh
        lastRecompLow  := vpSessLow
    else
        accumulateCurrentBar()

    // Publish current developing POC/VAH/VAL on EVERY confirmed bar so SMT
    // confluence (which evaluates `currDevPOC/VAH/VAL`) sees real values on
    // historical pivots, not just the realtime bar. Previously these were
    // only set inside the redraw block (gated by `barstate.islast`), which
    // meant historical SMT pivots saw `na` and silently skipped currDev
    // confluence — visible ★ only fired on iceberg detection (which runs
    // AFTER the redraw block) but never on SMT (which runs BEFORE).
    // Note: redraw block also computes these for its own histogram drawing.
    // Same values, minor duplication for clarity.
    if array.sum(vpBins) > 0
        [cPocIdx, cVaL, cVaH, _cTotal] = computeProfile(vpBins, vpRows, vpValueAreaP)
        float cBinSize = (vpSessHigh - vpSessLow) / vpRows
        currDevPOC := vpSessLow + (cPocIdx + 0.5) * cBinSize
        currDevVAH := vpSessLow + (cVaH + 1) * cBinSize
        currDevVAL := vpSessLow + cVaL * cBinSize

    // Developing POC trail — find this-bar's POC and append to the trail.
    if vpDevPocTrail
        int   barPocIdx = 0
        float barMaxV   = 0.0
        for i = 0 to vpRows - 1
            float v = array.get(vpBins, i)
            if v > barMaxV
                barMaxV   := v
                barPocIdx := i
        if barMaxV > 0
            float barBinSize = (vpSessHigh - vpSessLow) / vpRows
            float barPocPrice = vpSessLow + (barPocIdx + 0.5) * barBinSize
            array.push(pocTrailPoints, chart.point.from_index(bar_index, barPocPrice))

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 5) Redraw developing profile on the chart's last bar.
//    Gated so we only delete-and-rebuild the histogram boxes when something
//    actually changed: (a) initial load, (b) bar advanced (new bar's first
//    execution), or (c) the bar just closed and bins were updated. On a fast
//    intraday chart this drops ~99% of redundant redraws while still keeping
//    the histogram current.
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
vpHasData = array.sum(vpBins) > 0
vpShouldRedraw = barstate.islast and (na(lastVpDrawBar) or bar_index != lastVpDrawBar or barstate.isconfirmed)
if vpShouldRedraw and vpEnabled and vpHasData and not na(vpSessHigh) and vpSessHigh > vpSessLow
    lastVpDrawBar := bar_index
    // ── Cleanup current developing drawings ──────────────────────────────
    if array.size(vpBoxes) > 0
        for j = 0 to array.size(vpBoxes) - 1
            box.delete(array.get(vpBoxes, j))
        array.clear(vpBoxes)
    if array.size(vpSentBoxes) > 0
        for j = 0 to array.size(vpSentBoxes) - 1
            box.delete(array.get(vpSentBoxes, j))
        array.clear(vpSentBoxes)
    if array.size(vpHVNLines) > 0
        for j = 0 to array.size(vpHVNLines) - 1
            line.delete(array.get(vpHVNLines, j))
        array.clear(vpHVNLines)
    if array.size(vpHVNZoneBoxes) > 0
        for j = 0 to array.size(vpHVNZoneBoxes) - 1
            box.delete(array.get(vpHVNZoneBoxes, j))
        array.clear(vpHVNZoneBoxes)
    if array.size(vpHeatmapBoxes) > 0
        for j = 0 to array.size(vpHeatmapBoxes) - 1
            box.delete(array.get(vpHeatmapBoxes, j))
        array.clear(vpHeatmapBoxes)
    if array.size(vpBinLabels) > 0
        for j = 0 to array.size(vpBinLabels) - 1
            label.delete(array.get(vpBinLabels, j))
        array.clear(vpBinLabels)
    if not na(pocTrailPolyline)
        polyline.delete(pocTrailPolyline)
        pocTrailPolyline := na
    if not na(vpPocLine)
        line.delete(vpPocLine)
    if not na(vpVahLine)
        line.delete(vpVahLine)
    if not na(vpValLine)
        line.delete(vpValLine)
    if not na(vpPocLabel)
        label.delete(vpPocLabel)
    if not na(vpVahLabel)
        label.delete(vpVahLabel)
    if not na(vpValLabel)
        label.delete(vpValLabel)
    if not na(vpHighLabel)
        label.delete(vpHighLabel)
    if not na(vpLowLabel)
        label.delete(vpLowLabel)

    // ── Compute profile metrics ─────────────────────────────────────────
    [dPocIdx, dVaL, dVaH, dTotalV] = computeProfile(vpBins, vpRows, vpValueAreaP)

    float maxBinVol = 0.0
    float maxAbsBBP = 0.0
    for i = 0 to vpRows - 1
        float v = array.get(vpBins, i)
        if v > maxBinVol
            maxBinVol := v
        float bbp = math.abs(2.0 * array.get(vpBinsBull, i) - v)
        if bbp > maxAbsBBP
            maxAbsBBP := bbp

    float binSize  = (vpSessHigh - vpSessLow) / vpRows
    float pocPrice = vpSessLow + (dPocIdx + 0.5) * binSize
    float vahPrice = vpSessLow + (dVaH + 1) * binSize
    float valPrice = vpSessLow + dVaL * binSize

    currDevPOC := pocPrice
    currDevVAH := vahPrice
    currDevVAL := valPrice

    // ── Layout: single histogram OR twin (sentiment + volume) ───────────
    bool   twinMode      = vpProfileLayout == 'Twin (Volume + Sentiment)'
    int    halfWidth     = math.max(2, vpHistWidth / 2 - 1)
    int    profileLeftBar  = bar_index + 1

    // In Twin mode: sentiment on the LEFT (closer to chart), volume on the
    // RIGHT (further out). In Single mode: only the volume histogram is drawn.
    int sentLeftBar  = profileLeftBar
    int sentRightCap = profileLeftBar + halfWidth
    int volLeftBar   = twinMode ? sentRightCap + 2 : profileLeftBar
    int volRightCap  = volLeftBar + (twinMode ? halfWidth : vpHistWidth)
    int profileRightCap = volRightCap   // for the right-edge labels

    int lineLeft  = safeLeftBar(vpSessStart)   // v3.6: clamp — RE10026 guard on 1-min charts
    int lineRight = bar_index

    // ── Reset HVN/LVN counts so the dashboard reflects current profile ─
    hvnCount := 0
    lvnCount := 0

    // ── Per-bin loop: sentiment box + volume box + HVN/LVN + bin labels ─
    if maxBinVol > 0
        for i = 0 to vpRows - 1
            float v = array.get(vpBins, i)
            if v > 0
                float vBull = array.get(vpBinsBull, i)
                float vBear = v - vBull
                float bbp   = vBull - vBear       // signed net pressure
                float LpM   = v / maxBinVol       // ratio to POC bin
                float DpM   = maxAbsBBP > 0 ? math.abs(bbp) / maxAbsBBP : 0.0

                float binLowPrice  = vpSessLow + i * binSize
                float binHighPrice = binLowPrice + binSize
                float binMidPrice  = binLowPrice + binSize * 0.5

                // ── Sentiment histogram bin (twin layout only) ──────────
                // Don't force a minimum width — let near-balanced bins be
                // visually quiet rather than rounded up to a misleading 1-bar
                // box.
                if twinMode and vpShowHist and DpM > 0
                    int sentBarW = math.round(DpM * halfWidth)
                    if sentBarW > 0
                        color sentColor = bbp > 0 ? vpTwinSentBull : bbp < 0 ? vpTwinSentBear : vpNeutralBinColor
                        box sb = box.new(sentLeftBar, binHighPrice, sentLeftBar + sentBarW, binLowPrice, border_color = na, bgcolor = sentColor)
                        array.push(vpSentBoxes, sb)

                // ── Resolve the bin's base color (sentiment, VA, or twin neutral) ──
                color baseBinColor = vpOutFill
                if twinMode
                    baseBinColor := vpTwinVolColor    // neutral — sentiment shown separately
                else if vpSentiment
                    baseBinColor := bbp > 0 ? vpBullBinColor : bbp < 0 ? vpBearBinColor : vpNeutralBinColor
                else
                    bool inVA = i >= dVaL and i <= dVaH
                    baseBinColor := inVA ? vpVaFill : vpOutFill

                // Optional gradient: fade low-volume bins, saturate POC bin.
                color volColor = baseBinColor
                if vpGradientBins
                    color faintVersion = color.new(baseBinColor, 90)
                    volColor := color.from_gradient(LpM, 0.0, 1.0, faintVersion, baseBinColor)

                // ── Heatmap overlay (full-session per-bin shading) ─────
                // Drawn BEFORE the right-side histogram bin so it sits at
                // background depth on the chart proper. Spans session-start
                // to current bar.
                if vpHeatmap
                    color heatColor = color.new(volColor, vpHeatmapOpacity)
                    box hmb = box.new(lineLeft, binHighPrice, lineRight, binLowPrice, border_color = na, bgcolor = heatColor)
                    array.push(vpHeatmapBoxes, hmb)

                // ── Volume histogram bin (right-side profile) ──────────
                int volBarW = math.round(LpM * (twinMode ? halfWidth : vpHistWidth))
                if vpShowHist and volBarW > 0
                    box vb = box.new(volLeftBar, binHighPrice, volLeftBar + volBarW, binLowPrice, border_color = na, bgcolor = volColor)
                    array.push(vpBoxes, vb)

                    // ── Per-bin volume label (optional) ─────────────────
                    if vpShowBinLabels
                        float pctOfSess = dTotalV > 0 ? v / dTotalV * 100.0 : 0.0
                        string binText = str.tostring(v, format.volume) + ' (' + str.tostring(pctOfSess, '#.##') + '%)'
                        label bl = label.new(volLeftBar + volBarW, binMidPrice, binText, style = label.style_none, textcolor = chart.fg_color, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_left)
                        array.push(vpBinLabels, bl)

                // ── HVN / LVN markers (skip the POC bin) ────────────────
                // Two styles: Line (thin midpoint marker, default) or Zone
                // (full-width box across the session at the bin's price
                // range — LuxAlgo-style consolidation zone). Both use
                // extend.none — these are session-bound markers, not
                // forward-reference levels.
                if vpShowHVN and i != dPocIdx
                    if LpM >= vpHVNThreshold
                        hvnCount += 1
                        if vpHVNStyle == 'Zone'
                            box hZone = box.new(lineLeft, binHighPrice, lineRight, binLowPrice, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(vpHVNColor, vpHVNZoneOpacity))
                            array.push(vpHVNZoneBoxes, hZone)
                        else
                            line hl = line.new(lineLeft, binMidPrice, lineRight, binMidPrice, color = vpHVNColor, width = 1, style = line.style_solid, extend = extend.none)
                            array.push(vpHVNLines, hl)
                    else if LpM <= vpLVNThreshold
                        lvnCount += 1
                        if vpHVNStyle == 'Zone'
                            box lZone = box.new(lineLeft, binHighPrice, lineRight, binLowPrice, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(vpLVNColor, vpLVNZoneOpacity))
                            array.push(vpHVNZoneBoxes, lZone)
                        else
                            line ll = line.new(lineLeft, binMidPrice, lineRight, binMidPrice, color = vpLVNColor, width = 1, style = line.style_dotted, extend = extend.none)
                            array.push(vpHVNLines, ll)

    // ── POC / VAH / VAL across-session lines ─────────────────────────────
    if vpShowPOC
        vpPocLine := line.new(lineLeft, pocPrice, lineRight, pocPrice, color = vpPocColor, width = 2, extend = vpExtend ? extend.right : extend.none)
    if vpShowVA
        vpVahLine := line.new(lineLeft, vahPrice, lineRight, vahPrice, color = vpVaColor, width = 1, style = line.style_dashed, extend = vpExtend ? extend.right : extend.none)
        vpValLine := line.new(lineLeft, valPrice, lineRight, valPrice, color = vpVaColor, width = 1, style = line.style_dashed, extend = vpExtend ? extend.right : extend.none)

    // ── Right-edge POC/VAH/VAL price labels ──────────────────────────────
    if vpShowLabels
        int priceLabelBar = profileRightCap + 2
        if vpShowPOC
            vpPocLabel := label.new(priceLabelBar, pocPrice, 'POC ' + str.tostring(pocPrice, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = vpPocColor, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
        if vpShowVA
            vpVahLabel := label.new(priceLabelBar, vahPrice, 'VAH ' + str.tostring(vahPrice, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = vpVaColor, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
            vpValLabel := label.new(priceLabelBar, valPrice, 'VAL ' + str.tostring(valPrice, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = vpVaColor, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)

    // ── Profile-edge labels: Profile High / Profile Low ─────────────────
    if vpShowEdgeLabels and vpSessHigh > 0
        float rangePct = (vpSessHigh - vpSessLow) / vpSessLow * 100.0
        string totalLabel = vpSource == 'Money Flow' ? 'Total Money Flow: ' : 'Total Volume: '
        string highTip = 'Profile High — ' + str.tostring(vpSessHigh, format.mintick) + '\n' + str.tostring(rangePct, '#.##') + '% above Profile Low\n' + totalLabel + str.tostring(dTotalV, format.volume) + '\nBars: ' + str.tostring(vpSessBarCount)
        string lowTip  = 'Profile Low — '  + str.tostring(vpSessLow,  format.mintick) + '\n' + str.tostring(rangePct, '#.##') + '% below Profile High\n' + totalLabel + str.tostring(dTotalV, format.volume) + '\nBars: ' + str.tostring(vpSessBarCount)
        vpHighLabel := label.new(lineRight, vpSessHigh, str.tostring(vpSessHigh, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_down, color = color.new(vpPocColor, 30), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small, tooltip = highTip)
        vpLowLabel  := label.new(lineRight, vpSessLow,  str.tostring(vpSessLow,  format.mintick), style = label.style_label_up,   color = color.new(vpPocColor, 30), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small, tooltip = lowTip)

    // ── Developing POC trail polyline ───────────────────────────────────
    // Draws a connected line showing how the POC migrated bar-by-bar
    // through the session — buyer/seller value-building narrative.
    if vpDevPocTrail and array.size(pocTrailPoints) > 1
        pocTrailPolyline := polyline.new(pocTrailPoints, false, false, xloc.bar_index, vpDevPocColor, color(na), line.style_solid, 2)

//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ICEBERG / ABSORPTION DETECTION
//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// True iceberg orders need order-book data Pine cannot access. This is the
// standard proxy: a bar with abnormally high volume but a narrow range,
// closing at one extreme, has effectively "absorbed" supply or demand at a
// single price — the footprint a resting iceberg leaves on a candlestick.

// Top-level (non-conditional) so warmup is correct. We use the [1]-offset
// trailing values — i.e., SMA and ATR computed through the PREVIOUS bar — so
// the current bar's own volume/range doesn't dilute the threshold it's being
// compared against. (A 2× volume spike was previously raising its own SMA,
// causing the actual ratio to fall just under iceVolMult.)
volSMA = ta.sma(volume, 20)[1]
atr14  = ta.atr(14)[1]

// Reset session counter on the same anchor as VP.
if isNewVPSession
    iceCount := 0

// v3.2: pre-compute the iceberg confluence string at top-level — restored
// the v1.5/v2.8 hoist that v2.9 had moved inside the conditional.
// Backstory: `levelsInBar` IS a pure read function (no var, no ta.*) and
// the values it returns are correct whether it's called every bar or only
// on iceberg-firing bars. That part of v2.9's reasoning was correct, and
// the output IS unchanged in either placement. But Pine v6 still emits
// "function should be called on each calculation for consistency" as a
// style/conservative warning for ANY user-defined function that reads
// historical series via [barOffset] when called conditionally — pure or
// not. v2.9 bet that Pine wouldn't fire the warning for pure functions.
// It does. Hoisting back trades a microscopic per-bar string-concat cost
// (well below Pine's loop budget) for a clean editor experience. Output
// and behaviour unchanged in either placement.
string iceConfluence = levelsInBar(low, high, 0)

if iceEnabled and barstate.isconfirmed and not na(volSMA) and volSMA > 0 and not na(atr14) and atr14 > 0
    float barRange = high - low
    if barRange > 0
        bool volSpike   = volume > iceVolMult * volSMA
        bool narrowRange = barRange < iceRangeMult * atr14
        bool closeHigh  = close >= high - iceCloseThreshold * barRange
        bool closeLow   = close <= low  + iceCloseThreshold * barRange

        // Mutually exclusive — at iceCloseThreshold = 0.5 a doji bar (close
        // exactly at midpoint) would satisfy BOTH closeHigh AND closeLow.
        // Skip both rather than arbitrarily picking Bull, since a midpoint
        // close is genuinely ambiguous (neither side absorbed).
        bool isBullIce = volSpike and narrowRange and closeHigh and not closeLow
        bool isBearIce = volSpike and narrowRange and closeLow  and not closeHigh

        if isBullIce or isBearIce
            string confluence = iceConfluence   // pre-computed at top-level (v3.2)
            bool hasConf  = str.length(confluence) > 0
            int  confCount = hasConf ? countConfluenceTags(confluence) : 0
            if not iceRequireConf or hasConf
                bool   isBull = isBullIce
                color  c      = isBull ? iceBullColor : iceBearColor
                float  yPos   = isBull ? low : high
                string typeS  = isBull ? 'Bull' : 'Bear'
                // v3.0: ★N strength count on the iceberg label instead of plain ★.
                string txt    = iceMarkerText + (hasConf ? ' ★' + str.tostring(confCount) : '')
                string tip    = 'Iceberg ' + typeS + ' Absorption\n' + 'Volume: ' + str.tostring(volume / volSMA, '#.#') + 'x avg\n' + 'Range: ' + str.tostring(barRange / atr14, '#.##') + ' ATR\n' + 'Close: ' + str.tostring((close - low) / barRange * 100, '#') + '% of bar' + (hasConf ? '\n★ Confluence (' + str.tostring(confCount) + '): ' + confluence : '')
                label.new(bar_index, yPos, txt, style = isBull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = c, textcolor = color.white, size = getLabelSize(iceMarkerSize), tooltip = tip)

                iceCount         := iceCount + 1
                lastIceBar       := bar_index
                lastIceType      := typeS
                lastIceConf      := hasConf
                lastIceConfCount := confCount

                if iceAlertEnabled
                    alert(typeS + 'ish Iceberg' + (hasConf ? ' | ★' + str.tostring(confCount) + ' ' + confluence : ''), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// DASHBOARD
//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
if showDash and barstate.islast
    if na(dashTable)
        dashTable := table.new(getDashPosition(dashPos), 2, 24, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 70), border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 60), frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(color.gray, 40))

    color hdrBg = color.new(color.gray, 50)
    color rowBg = color.new(color.black, 50)
    color lblTx = color.new(color.white, 0)

    // Header.
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 0, 'SMT+VP+Ice', text_color = color.white, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = hdrBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 0, 'v3.6',       text_color = color.new(color.white, 40), text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = hdrBg)

    // Current developing levels.
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 1, 'Curr POC', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 1, na(currDevPOC) ? '—' : str.tostring(currDevPOC, format.mintick), text_color = vpPocColor, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 2, 'Curr VAH', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 2, na(currDevVAH) ? '—' : str.tostring(currDevVAH, format.mintick), text_color = vpVaColor, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 3, 'Curr VAL', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 3, na(currDevVAL) ? '—' : str.tostring(currDevVAL, format.mintick), text_color = vpVaColor, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)

    // Previous session.
    string prevPocCell = na(prevSessPOC) ? '—' : str.tostring(prevSessPOC, format.mintick) + (na(prevSessPOCSentiment) or prevSessPOCSentiment == 'Neutral' ? '' : ' (' + prevSessPOCSentiment + ')')
    color  prevPocCol  = na(prevSessPOC) ? color.gray : (prevSessPOCSentiment == 'Bull' ? GREEN : prevSessPOCSentiment == 'Bear' ? RED : vpPrevPocColor)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 4, 'Prev POC', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 4, prevPocCell, text_color = prevPocCol, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 5, 'Prev VAH', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 5, na(prevSessVAH) ? '—' : str.tostring(prevSessVAH, format.mintick), text_color = vpPrevVaColor,  text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 6, 'Prev VAL', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 6, na(prevSessVAL) ? '—' : str.tostring(prevSessVAL, format.mintick), text_color = vpPrevVaColor,  text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)

    // Composite (multi-session aggregate) levels — v3.0. Suffixed with the
    // session count (e.g., '1.34000 [5]') so the user can see how many
    // sessions the aggregate is built from. Shows '—' until at least one
    // session has been finalized after script load.
    int compSessCount = matrix.rows(compositeSessionBins)
    string compPocCell = na(compositePOC) ? '—' : str.tostring(compositePOC, format.mintick) + ' [' + str.tostring(compSessCount) + ']'
    string compVahCell = na(compositeVAH) ? '—' : str.tostring(compositeVAH, format.mintick)
    string compValCell = na(compositeVAL) ? '—' : str.tostring(compositeVAL, format.mintick)
    color  compPocCol  = na(compositePOC) ? color.gray : vpCompositePocColor
    color  compVaCol   = na(compositeVAH) ? color.gray : vpCompositeVaColor
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 7, 'Comp POC', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 7, compPocCell, text_color = compPocCol, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 8, 'Comp VAH', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 8, compVahCell, text_color = compVaCol, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 9, 'Comp VAL', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 9, compValCell, text_color = compVaCol, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)

    // Price vs prior Value Area.
    string vaPosTxt = '—'
    color  vaPosCol = color.gray
    if not na(prevSessVAH) and not na(prevSessVAL)
        if close > prevSessVAH
            vaPosTxt := 'Above'
            vaPosCol := GREEN
        else if close < prevSessVAL
            vaPosTxt := 'Below'
            vaPosCol := RED
        else
            vaPosTxt := 'Inside'
            vaPosCol := GOLD
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 10, 'Price vs pVA', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 10, vaPosTxt, text_color = vaPosCol, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)

    // AVWAP and σ levels (current bar — uses live projection).
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 11, 'AVWAP', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 11, na(avwap) ? '—' : str.tostring(avwap, format.mintick), text_color = avwapColor, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 12, '±' + str.tostring(sigma1Mult, '#.#') + 'σ', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 12, na(avwapU1) ? '—' : str.tostring(avwapL1, format.mintick) + ' / ' + str.tostring(avwapU1, format.mintick), text_color = sigma1Color, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 13, '±' + str.tostring(sigma2Mult, '#.#') + 'σ', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 13, na(avwapU2) ? '—' : str.tostring(avwapL2, format.mintick) + ' / ' + str.tostring(avwapU2, format.mintick), text_color = sigma2Color, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    // ±3σ row added in v2.8. Shows '—' when σ3 toggle is off, matching
    // how other disabled features render in the dashboard.
    string sig3Val = showSigma3 and not na(avwapU3) ? str.tostring(avwapL3, format.mintick) + ' / ' + str.tostring(avwapU3, format.mintick) : '—'
    color  sig3Col = showSigma3 ? sigma3Color : color.gray
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 14, '±' + str.tostring(sigma3Mult, '#.#') + 'σ', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 14, sig3Val, text_color = sig3Col, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)

    // Naked POC count.
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 15, 'Naked POCs', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 15, str.tostring(array.size(nakedPOCs)), text_color = nPocColor, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)

    // Last SMT events. v3.0: ★N strength-count suffix when confluence fires.
    string bullTxt = na(lastBullBar) ? '—' : lastBullSym + ' (' + str.tostring(bar_index - lastBullBar) + ' bars ago)' + (lastBullConf ? ' ★' + str.tostring(lastBullConfCount) : '')
    string bearTxt = na(lastBearBar) ? '—' : lastBearSym + ' (' + str.tostring(bar_index - lastBearBar) + ' bars ago)' + (lastBearConf ? ' ★' + str.tostring(lastBearConfCount) : '')
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 16, 'Last Bull SMT', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 16, bullTxt, text_color = bullColor, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 17, 'Last Bear SMT', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 17, bearTxt, text_color = bearColor, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)

    // Iceberg / absorption stats.
    string iceTxt = na(lastIceBar) ? '—' : lastIceType + ' (' + str.tostring(bar_index - lastIceBar) + ' bars ago)' + (lastIceConf ? ' ★' + str.tostring(lastIceConfCount) : '')
    color  iceCol = na(lastIceBar) ? color.gray : (lastIceType == 'Bull' ? iceBullColor : iceBearColor)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 18, 'Icebergs (sess)', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 18, str.tostring(iceCount), text_color = iceCount > 0 ? color.white : color.gray, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 19, 'Last Iceberg', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 19, iceTxt, text_color = iceCol, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)

    // Session sentiment summary (developing-session bull/bear split).
    float sessTotal = array.sum(vpBins)
    float sessBull  = array.sum(vpBinsBull)
    float bullPct   = sessTotal > 0 ? sessBull / sessTotal * 100 : na
    string sentTxt  = na(bullPct) ? '—' : str.tostring(bullPct, '#') + '% Bull / ' + str.tostring(100 - bullPct, '#') + '% Bear'
    color  sentCol  = na(bullPct) ? color.gray : (bullPct >= 55 ? GREEN : bullPct <= 45 ? RED : GOLD)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 20, 'Sentiment', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 20, sentTxt, text_color = sentCol, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)

    // HVN / LVN counts (developing-session). Shows '—' if HVN tracking is off.
    string hvnTxt = vpShowHVN ? str.tostring(hvnCount) + ' / ' + str.tostring(lvnCount) : '—'
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 21, 'HVN / LVN', text_color = lblTx, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 21, hvnTxt, text_color = vpShowHVN ? color.white : color.gray, text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)

    // Footer hint.
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 22, 'Session',  text_color = color.new(color.white, 40), text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 22, vpAnchorIn, text_color = color.new(color.white, 40), text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 0, 23, '★N = N confluences', text_color = color.new(color.white, 50), text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)
    table.cell(dashTable, 1, 23, '', text_color = color.new(color.white, 50), text_size = dashTxtSz, bgcolor = rowBg)

//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ANCHORED VWAP — PLOTS
//══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Break the line at session boundaries by plotting na on the first bar of
// a new session. The AVWAP value itself is correctly reset above, but Pine's
// plot() would otherwise connect last-bar-of-prev-session to first-bar-of-new.
plotAvwap = avwapEnabled and not isNewVPSession ? avwap   : na
plotU1    = avwapEnabled and showSigma1 and not isNewVPSession ? avwapU1 : na
plotL1    = avwapEnabled and showSigma1 and not isNewVPSession ? avwapL1 : na
plotU2    = avwapEnabled and showSigma2 and not isNewVPSession ? avwapU2 : na
plotL2    = avwapEnabled and showSigma2 and not isNewVPSession ? avwapL2 : na
plotU3    = avwapEnabled and showSigma3 and not isNewVPSession ? avwapU3 : na
plotL3    = avwapEnabled and showSigma3 and not isNewVPSession ? avwapL3 : na

avwapPlot = plot(plotAvwap, 'AVWAP',    color = avwapColor,  linewidth = avwapWidth)
u1Plot    = plot(plotU1,    'AVWAP +1σ', color = sigma1Color, linewidth = 1)
l1Plot    = plot(plotL1,    'AVWAP -1σ', color = sigma1Color, linewidth = 1)
u2Plot    = plot(plotU2,    'AVWAP +2σ', color = sigma2Color, linewidth = 1)
l2Plot    = plot(plotL2,    'AVWAP -2σ', color = sigma2Color, linewidth = 1)
u3Plot    = plot(plotU3,    'AVWAP +3σ', color = sigma3Color, linewidth = 1)
l3Plot    = plot(plotL3,    'AVWAP -3σ', color = sigma3Color, linewidth = 1)

fill(u1Plot, l1Plot, color = fillBands and showSigma1 ? color.new(sigma1Color, fillOpacity) : na, title = '1σ Fill')
fill(u2Plot, u1Plot, color = fillBands and showSigma2 and showSigma1 ? color.new(sigma2Color, fillOpacity) : na, title = 'Upper 1σ→2σ Fill')
fill(l1Plot, l2Plot, color = fillBands and showSigma2 and showSigma1 ? color.new(sigma2Color, fillOpacity) : na, title = 'Lower 1σ→2σ Fill')
fill(u3Plot, u2Plot, color = fillBands and showSigma3 and showSigma2 ? color.new(sigma3Color, fillOpacity) : na, title = 'Upper 2σ→3σ Fill')
fill(l2Plot, l3Plot, color = fillBands and showSigma3 and showSigma2 ? color.new(sigma3Color, fillOpacity) : na, title = 'Lower 2σ→3σ Fill')
